                  "textEn": "The main reason is that children are usually more impressionable than adults, so they tend to absorb catchy messages very easily. Bright colours, fun characters, repeated slogans, and cheerful music can all make an advertisement stick in their minds. In many cases, children soak things up like sponges, so even a simple ad can plant a seed and make a product seem exciting, desirable, or even essential. As a result, advertising often shapes not only their preferences, but also their behaviour.",
