                  "textEn": "Laws can help, but they cannot do everything on their own. If people keep buying products made from endangered animals, wasting natural resources, or treating wildlife as a source of profit, the problem will keep coming back. That is why schools, the media, and even social campaigns have a role to play. The more people understand that every species is a thread in the web of life, the more likely they are to act responsibly.",
                  "textZh": "法律固然有幫助，但單靠法律並不能解決所有問題。如果人們仍然繼續購買由瀕危動物製成的產品、浪費自然資源，或者把野生動物當成賺錢工具，那麼問題始終會一再出現。這就是為甚麼學校、媒體，甚至社會宣傳都扮演著重要角色。人們越明白每一個物種都是生命之網中的一條線，他們就越有可能作出負責任的行動。",
                  "pages": [
                    39
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    39,
                    39
                  ]
