                  "textEn": "Human beings rely on nature for food, medicine, clean water, and economic activities such as farming and fishing. If species vanish, we do not just lose part of nature; we also lose resources, resilience, and future possibilities. In a way, biodiversity is like a safety net. The richer and stronger it is, the better the planet can cope with pressure. If that net is torn apart, both nature and human society become more fragile.",
