                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "School should not just be about memorising facts or chasing marks. Children also need space to imagine, explore, and express what is going on in their minds. Art gives them that space. In a way, it opens a window into how they see the world. Some feelings are hard to put into words, especially for younger children, so drawing, painting, or making things with their hands can help them communicate in a more natural way. On top of that, art gives children a little room to breathe in an education system that can sometimes feel too exam-driven.",
