                  "textEn": "Art teaches patience, attention to detail, and the confidence to experiment. It also shows children that not everything has one fixed answer. In many academic subjects, there is a right or wrong response, whereas art allows more freedom and interpretation. That can be incredibly healthy, because real life is rarely black and white. Art also teaches children how to cope when things do not go to plan. Sometimes a mistake in an artwork turns into part of the final piece, which is a lovely reminder that setbacks do not always mean failure.",
