                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Sometimes people stay away from exhibitions because they assume they will be too quiet, too formal, or even a little intimidating. If that happens, it becomes an uphill battle to get people through the door. By contrast, if exhibitions include guided tours, interactive displays, multimedia elements, or simple explanations that bring the artwork to life, visitors are far more likely to feel connected. In other words, people are more easily drawn in when art feels alive rather than distant.",
                  "textZh": "有時候，人們不去看展覽，是因為他們先入為主地覺得展覽太安靜、太正式，甚至有點令人卻步。如果是這樣，要把人吸引進場就會變得相當困難。相反，如果展覽加入導賞、互動裝置、多媒體元素，或者一些能讓作品變得更容易理解的簡單說明，參觀者就會更容易產生連結。換句話說，當藝術給人的感覺是活生生的，而不是遙不可及的，人們自然更容易被吸引。",
