                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When people read a book, they have to picture the characters, settings, and emotions in their own minds, so reading is often a slower and more personal experience. A book can also go deeper into someone’s thoughts, background, and inner conflict. Films, by contrast, put everything right in front of you through images, sound, music, and acting, so they can hit you much more quickly. In a way, books ask the imagination to do more of the heavy lifting, while films bring the world to life for you straight away.",
