                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that business work often comes with heavy responsibility, tight deadlines, client pressure, and constant problem-solving. If a company is trying to grow, stay ahead of competitors, or keep major clients happy, the workload can snowball very quickly. On top of that, senior people are usually the ones who have to make the final call when something goes wrong. In other words, when the stakes are high, the hours often stretch.",
