                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, working long hours can sometimes look impressive on the surface, but it may hide deeper problems underneath. If people are always burning the candle at both ends, they are more likely to make poor decisions, lose focus, and wear themselves thin. In the long run, smart systems, good delegation, and clear priorities matter more than simply staying at the office for endless hours. So, while long hours may come with the territory from time to time, they should not become a badge of honour.",
