                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "A lot of small businesses fail because they try to grow too fast before they are truly ready. In my view, growth built on weak foundations is like building a house on sand. If the product is unreliable, the service is inconsistent, or the business does not stand for anything clear, expansion can quickly become a headache rather than a success story. That is why the early stage matters so much. A business needs to know what it does well, who it serves, and why customers should come back.",
