                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "A small business cannot survive on a good idea alone. The point is that the owner has to know what people actually need, what they are willing to pay for, and how to offer something that stands out from the crowd. On top of that, practical business skills such as budgeting, planning, pricing, and communication are absolutely essential. You can have the brightest idea in the room, but if you cannot manage money or build trust with customers, the business may never really get off the ground.",
                  "textZh": "一門小生意單靠一個好點子是無法生存的。重點在於，經營者必須知道人們真正需要甚麼、願意為甚麼付錢，以及如何提供一些能夠從眾多競爭者中突圍而出的東西。除此之外，像預算管理、計劃能力、定價，以及溝通這些實際商業技能，也絕對不可或缺。你可以擁有全場最亮眼的想法，但如果你不懂得管理金錢，或者無法和顧客建立信任，那門生意很可能根本無法真正起飛。",
