                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Starting a small business is rarely a smooth ride. Things can go wrong, sales can be slow, plans can fall through, and unexpected costs can appear out of nowhere. That is why resilience matters so much. A good business owner cannot fall apart every time something goes off script. They need to keep a cool head, learn from mistakes, and adjust quickly when the market changes. In a way, running a small business is a bit like steering a boat through changing weather: if you panic whenever the wind shifts, you are unlikely to stay on course.",
                  "textZh": "開一門小生意很少會是一帆風順的事情。事情可能出錯，銷售可能疲弱，計劃可能落空，而意想不到的支出也可能突然冒出來。這正是為甚麼韌性那麼重要。一位好的經營者不能每逢事情不如預期就先亂了陣腳。他們需要保持冷靜、從錯誤中學習，並且在市場變化時迅速調整。某程度上，經營小生意有點像在變幻天氣中掌舵：如果風向一轉你就慌了，你就很難保持航道。",
