                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that working for someone else usually gives people more stability, more structure, and more chances to learn the ropes. They can gain experience, build professional skills, and understand how a business actually works without having to shoulder all the risk themselves. In other words, it allows people to get their feet on the ground before they try to fly on their own. For most people, that is the safer and wiser path, because starting a business can be financially risky and emotionally draining.",
