                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "If nothing ever changed, life would become very stagnant. People might stay in their comfort zone, but they would also miss the chance to learn, improve, and see the world from a different angle. In that sense, change can be a breath of fresh air. It may feel uncomfortable at first, but it often pushes people to discover strengths they did not even know they had. So, to me, change is often the engine of personal development rather than something to fear by default.",
                  "textZh": "如果一切都永遠不變，人生其實很容易變得停滯不前。人們或許會一直留在舒適圈裡，但同時也會錯過學習、進步，以及用不同角度看世界的機會。從這個角度來看，改變就像一陣新鮮空氣。它一開始也許會令人不舒服，但很多時候，它正正會逼使人發現自己原本都不知道的能力。所以，在我看來，改變往往是個人成長的引擎，而不是理所當然需要害怕的東西。",
