          "categoryId": "city",
          "categoryTitle": "City",
          "pages": [
            5,
            6,
            7
          ],
          "pageRange": [
            5,
            7
          ],
          "cue": {
            "questionEn": "What are the advantages of living in a city?",
            "questionZh": "居住在城市裡有甚麼好處？",
            "raw": "Topic: What are the advantages of living in a city?\n居住在城市裡有甚麼好處？"
          },
          "responseModels": [
            {
              "number": 1,
              "labelEn": "Sample 1",
              "labelZh": "示範答案 1",
              "developmentOrder": [
                "idea",
                "explanation",
                "example",
                "conclusion"
              ],
              "steps": [
                {
                  "number": 1,
                  "sourceNumber": 1,
                  "stage": "idea",
                  "labelEn": "Idea",
                  "labelZh": "主旨",
                  "sourceLabel": "Idea",
                  "textEn": "I think one of the biggest advantages of living in a city is convenience, because so many essential services and facilities are right on your doorstep.",
                  "textZh": "我認為，住在城市其中一個最大的好處就是方便，因為很多基本服務和設施都近在咫尺。",
                  "pages": [
                    5
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    5,
                    5
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 2,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In a city, people usually have easier access to public transport, hospitals, schools, supermarkets, restaurants, and entertainment venues. That makes daily life smoother and far less time-consuming. Instead of bending over backwards just to get from one place to another, people can often get things done quickly and efficiently. In that sense, city life puts time back in your hands, and that can make a real difference, especially for people with busy schedules.",
                  "textZh": "在城市裡，人們通常更容易接觸到公共交通、醫院、學校、超市、餐廳，以及各種娛樂場所。這會令日常生活更加順暢，也不用花那麼多時間。人們不需要為了去不同地方而費盡周章，很多事情都可以更快、更有效率地完成。從這個角度來看，城市生活某程度上是把時間還給人，而這對生活忙碌的人來說尤其重要。",
                  "pages": [
                    5
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    5,
                    5
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "number": 3,
                  "sourceNumber": 3,
                  "stage": "example",
                  "labelEn": "Example",
                  "labelZh": "例子",
                  "sourceLabel": "Example",
                  "textEn": "For example, if someone lives in a large city, they may be able to commute by train, pick up groceries on the way home, and meet friends for dinner without travelling long distances. By contrast, in a less developed area, even simple errands can eat up half the day.",
                  "textZh": "例如，如果一個人住在大城市，他可能可以乘火車上下班、回家途中順便買菜，然後晚上再和朋友吃飯，而不需要花很長時間來回奔波。相比之下，在一些發展較少的地方，就連處理一些簡單瑣事，也可能耗掉半天時間。",
                  "pages": [
                    5
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    5,
                    5
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "number": 4,
                  "sourceNumber": 4,
                  "stage": "conclusion",
                  "labelEn": "Conclusion",
                  "labelZh": "總結",
                  "sourceLabel": "Conclusion",
                  "textEn": "So, I’d say convenience is a major advantage of city life, because it allows people to live more efficiently and with less friction in their daily routine.",
                  "textZh": "所以，我會說方便是城市生活的一大優勢，因為它能讓人以更有效率、也更少阻力的方式去過日常生活。",
                  "pages": [
                    5
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    5,
                    5
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "number": 2,
              "labelEn": "Sample 2",
              "labelZh": "示範答案 2",
              "developmentOrder": [
                "idea",
                "explanation",
                "example",
                "conclusion"
              ],
              "steps": [
                {
                  "number": 1,
                  "sourceNumber": 5,
                  "stage": "idea",
                  "labelEn": "Idea",
                  "labelZh": "主旨",
                  "sourceLabel": "Idea 2",
                  "textEn": "On top of that, living in a city often opens the door to better opportunities, both professionally and socially.",
                  "textZh": "除此之外，住在城市通常也能帶來更多機會，無論是在職業發展還是社交方面都是如此。",
                  "pages": [
                    6
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    6,
                    6
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 6,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Cities tend to be the beating heart of education, business, and culture. There are usually more jobs, more networking opportunities, and a wider range of courses, events, and experiences. As a result, people are more likely to broaden their horizons and grow as individuals. A city can be a bit like a crossroads: different industries, ideas, and people all meet there, and that creates an environment in which ambition has room to breathe.",
                  "textZh": "城市往往是一個地方在教育、商業和文化上的核心地帶。那裡通常有更多工作機會、更多建立人脈的機會，以及更廣泛的課程、活動和體驗。因此，人們更有可能開闊眼界，並在個人成長上走得更遠。城市有點像一個交匯點：不同的行業、想法和人都在那裡相遇，而這就形成了一個能讓理想與野心有空間發展的環境。",
                  "pages": [
                    6
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    6,
                    6
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "number": 3,
                  "sourceNumber": 7,
                  "stage": "example",
                  "labelEn": "Example",
                  "labelZh": "例子",
                  "sourceLabel": "Example 2",
                  "textEn": "For instance, a young graduate living in a city may find it much easier to attend interviews, take evening classes, go to professional events, and meet people from different backgrounds. That kind of exposure can work wonders, because it helps people build skills, confidence, and perspective all at once.",
                  "textZh": "例如，一位住在城市的年輕畢業生，通常會更容易參加面試、報讀晚間課程、出席專業活動，並接觸來自不同背景的人。這種接觸面往往很有幫助，因為它能同時提升一個人的能力、自信，以及看事情的角度。",
                  "pages": [
                    6
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    6,
                    6
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "number": 4,
                  "sourceNumber": 8,
                  "stage": "conclusion",
                  "labelEn": "Conclusion",
                  "labelZh": "總結",
                  "sourceLabel": "Conclusion 2",
                  "textEn": "Overall, I’d say the main advantages of living in a city are convenience and opportunity. Granted, city life can sometimes feel fast-paced or even overwhelming, but it undeniably gives people better access to resources, connections, and the kind of experiences that can help them move forward in life.",
                  "textZh": "總結來說，我會說住在城市的主要好處在於它既方便，又充滿機會。雖然城市生活有時節奏很快，甚至會讓人喘不過氣，但它確實能讓人更容易接觸資源、建立連結，並追求自己想要的生活。",
                  "pages": [
                    7
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    7,
                    7
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
