                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, crowded cities can sometimes feel like a pressure cooker. People are always rushing, always queuing, always dealing with noise and pressure, so they may become impatient, emotionally tired, or less connected to the people around them. There is also a strange paradox there: a person can be in the middle of a sea of people and still feel completely alone. When life moves at breakneck speed, it becomes harder to build strong community ties or simply slow down long enough to enjoy life.",
