                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In many crowded cities, the real problem is not just the number of people; it is the gap between population growth and infrastructure. If housing is unaffordable, public transport is unreliable, and medical or educational services are overloaded, daily life starts to feel like a grind. Governments therefore need to build more affordable housing, improve transport networks, and make sure essential services can keep pace with demand. Otherwise, people end up paying more, travelling longer, and living under constant pressure.",
                  "textZh": "在很多擠迫城市裡，真正的問題不只是人口多，而是人口增長和基建發展之間出現落差。如果住屋難以負擔、公共交通不可靠，而醫療或教育服務又不堪重負，日常生活就會變成一場消耗戰。所以，政府需要興建更多可負擔房屋、改善交通網絡，並確保基本公共服務能跟得上需求。否則，人們就會變成花更多錢、花更長時間通勤，還要長期承受壓力。",
