                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "A city should not feel like a concrete jungle where people simply squeeze through life. Even in a densely populated place, governments can improve well-being by adding parks, controlling pollution, protecting pedestrian areas, and providing community facilities. Living standards are not measured by income alone; they also depend on whether people have space to rest, clean air to breathe, and a neighbourhood that feels safe and livable. In other words, a good city should do more than function; it should allow people to live with dignity.",
                  "textZh": "一座城市不應該像鋼筋水泥森林一樣，讓人只能在夾縫中勉強生活。即使在高密度地區，政府仍然可以透過增加公園、控制污染、保障行人空間，以及提供社區設施來改善市民福祉。生活質素並不只是看收入高低，還取決於人們是否有空間休息、有乾淨空氣可以呼吸，以及是否身處一個安全而宜居的社區。換句話說，一個好的城市不應只是能運作而已；它更應該讓人活得有尊嚴。",
