                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The reason is that traffic is often a major source of urban air pollution, especially in busy cities where the roads are constantly clogged up. If more people take public transport, walk, cycle, or carpool, fewer vehicles will be pumping exhaust fumes into the air. In other words, cleaner commuting can help take some of the smoke out of the city’s lungs.",
                  "textZh": "原因是交通往往是城市空氣污染的主要來源之一，尤其是在道路長期擠塞的繁忙城市裡更是如此。如果更多人乘搭公共交通、步行、踩單車，或者共乘車輛，路上排放廢氣的汽車就會減少。換句話說，更潔淨的出行方式可以幫助城市的「肺」少吸一點煙霧。",
                  "pages": [
                    14
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    14,
                    14
                  ]
