                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Air pollution does not only come from traffic; it is also linked to the way people consume energy and handle waste. If people save electricity, use energy-efficient appliances, avoid unnecessary packaging, and support greener businesses, they can help reduce pollution further up the chain. It may not look dramatic at first glance, but when thousands or even millions of people make greener choices, the effect can snowball.",
                  "textZh": "空氣污染不只是來自交通，它也和人們如何使用能源，以及怎樣處理廢物有關。如果人們節省用電、使用節能電器、避免不必要的包裝，並支持較環保的商店或企業，他們其實可以從源頭鏈的更上游減少污染。這些改變乍看之下未必很震撼，但當成千上萬，甚至數以百萬計的人都作出較環保的選擇時，效果就會像雪球一樣愈滾愈大。",
