                  "textEn": "Building high-rise structures usually requires heavier investment, stronger infrastructure, and more complex planning. You may need better roads, more advanced utilities, lifts, safety systems, and long-term maintenance. In many rural areas, that would be overkill. On top of that, the countryside is often valued for its open views, slower pace of life, and closer connection to nature, so a forest of tall buildings would look a bit out of place.",
