                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In some places, tall buildings clearly have strong advantages. When land is limited and population density is high, building upwards can be the most practical solution. Tall buildings can provide more homes, more office space, and more facilities without swallowing up too much land. In that sense, they can help a city make more out of less. That said, height by itself is not a magic wand. If towers are badly planned, they can create congestion, put pressure on transport and public services, and make urban life feel more cramped rather than more comfortable.",
                  "textZh": "在某些地方，高樓的確有很明顯的優勢。當土地有限，而人口密度又很高時，向上發展往往是最實際的解決方法。高樓可以在不大量吞噬土地的情況下，提供更多住宅、辦公空間，以及其他設施。從這個角度來看，它能幫助城市用更少的土地做到更多事情。不過，單單「高」本身並不是萬能藥。如果規劃做得不好，高樓也可能造成擠塞、加重交通和公共服務的壓力，並令城市生活變得更侷促，而不是更舒適。",
