                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Low-rise areas are often easier to navigate, less visually overwhelming, and more closely connected to neighbourhood life. They can preserve local character, allow more sunlight into the streets, and make communities feel less anonymous. A city full of towers may look impressive on paper, but if it starts to feel like a forest of concrete, something important can be lost. Sometimes smaller buildings give a place more warmth, more identity, and more breathing room.",
                  "textZh": "低層建築區通常更容易穿梭，不會在視覺上帶來那麼強的壓迫感，而且與社區生活的連結也往往更緊密。它們可以保留地方特色，讓街道有更多陽光，也令社區不會那麼陌生冷淡。一座滿是高塔的城市，紙面上看起來也許很壯觀，但如果它開始讓人感覺像一片鋼筋水泥森林，那就可能失去一些很重要的東西。有時候，小型建築反而能帶來更多溫度、更多個性，以及更多喘息空間。",
