                  "labelZh": "總結",
                  "sourceLabel": "Conclusion 2",
                  "textEn": "Overall, I would not say tall buildings are automatically more beneficial than small buildings. Tall buildings work well when a city needs efficiency and density, whereas small buildings often shine when livability, community, and local character matter more. So, to me, the best answer is not “the taller, the better,” but “the right building for the right place.”",
                  "textZh": "總結來說，我不會說高樓一定比小型建築更有好處。當一座城市需要效率和高密度發展時，高樓會發揮很大作用；而當宜居性、社區感，以及地方特色更重要時，小型建築往往更有優勢。所以，在我看來，最好的答案不是「越高越好」，而是「合適的地方，配合合適的建築」。",
