                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "In many cases, if a place is packed, people assume there must be a good reason for it. They may see it as a sign that the food is better, the event is more exciting, or the overall experience is more worthwhile. On top of that, crowded places make it easier to meet friends, people-watch, or simply avoid the feeling of being alone. For some people, a crowd is not a nuisance; it is social proof that they are in the right place.",
