                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Good public spaces give people opportunities to mix, interact, and feel connected to the place where they live. A city without leisure facilities may still function, but it can feel cold, impersonal, and built only for efficiency. By contrast, when a city has lively parks, sports grounds, waterfront areas, or cultural entertainment venues, it feels as though the city has a heartbeat rather than just a traffic system. These places help turn a collection of buildings into a real community.",
                  "textZh": "良好的公共空間能讓人有機會交流、互動，並對自己居住的地方產生連結。沒有休閒設施的城市也許仍然可以運作，但它往往會令人感到冰冷、缺乏人情味，彷彿只是為了效率而建。相比之下，當一座城市擁有有活力的公園、運動場、海濱空間，或者文化娛樂場所時，它就會讓人覺得這座城市有脈搏，而不只是有交通系統。這些地方能把一堆建築物，慢慢變成真正的社區。",
