                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Without proper planning, a city can grow in a messy and haphazard way. Roads become congested, housing becomes unbalanced, and public services struggle to keep up. Good urban planning, by contrast, gives a city a backbone. It helps governments decide where homes, transport links, schools, hospitals, and business areas should go, so that the city does not simply grow bigger, but grows better. In other words, urban planning is not just about drawing lines on a map; it is about making daily life more workable and less chaotic.",
