                  "sourceNumber": 8,
                  "stage": "conclusion",
                  "labelEn": "Conclusion",
                  "labelZh": "總結",
                  "sourceLabel": "Conclusion 2",
                  "textEn": "Overall, I’d say clothing fashion in Hong Kong has changed from being more formal and predictable to being more casual, global, and individualistic. That said, the old and the new still go hand in hand, because in professional or traditional settings, people still value neatness, polish, and a sense of occasion.",
                  "textZh": "總結來說，我會說香港的服裝時尚已經由一種較正式、較可預測的狀態，轉變成更休閒、更全球化，也更重視個人風格的面貌。不過，舊與新至今仍然並肩而行，因為在專業場合或傳統場合裡，人們仍然很重視整齊、得體，以及場合感。",
                  "pages": [
                    60
                  ],
