                  "textEn": "I think that often comes down to budget, taste, and personality. Some people love hunting for bargains, while others want something less mass-produced and more distinctive. A small boutique may offer clothes with more character, and a second-hand shop can feel like a treasure hunt rather than a routine purchase. On top of that, with growing awareness of sustainability, some people are becoming more careful about buying fewer but better items, or giving pre-owned clothes a second life.",
