                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In many places, including Hong Kong, men’s fashion has often been more straightforward and functional, whereas women’s fashion tends to be broader, more detailed, and more trend-driven. Men are often expected to keep things simple, neat, and practical, so their choices may revolve around comfort, fit, and convenience. Women, by contrast, are often encouraged to pay more attention to colour, cut, texture, and accessories. In that sense, men’s clothing is sometimes treated as a tool, while women’s clothing is seen more as a language.",
                  "textZh": "在很多地方，包括香港，男性時裝往往較直接、較功能性；相反，女性時裝通常更廣泛、更講究細節，也更受潮流帶動。男性常常被期待穿得簡單、整齊、實用，因此他們的選擇多半圍繞舒適度、合身程度，以及方便與否。相比之下，女性則往往被鼓勵更留意顏色、剪裁、質感，以及配飾。從這個角度來說，男性的衣著有時像是一種工具，而女性的衣著則更像一種語言。",
