                  "stage": "conclusion",
                  "labelEn": "Conclusion",
                  "labelZh": "總結",
                  "sourceLabel": "Conclusion 2",
                  "textEn": "Overall, I’d say uniforms can work very well when they serve a clear purpose and are designed with people in mind. They can promote equality, professionalism, and team spirit, which are real strengths. But if they ignore comfort or individuality, they risk becoming less like a shared identity and more like a straitjacket.",
                  "textZh": "總結來說，我會說，只要制服有清楚的目的，而且設計時有真正把人的需要放在心上，它們其實可以運作得很好。它們可以帶來平等感、專業形象，以及團隊精神，這些都是真正的優點。不過，如果制服忽視了舒適感或個人特質，它就有可能不再像是一種共同身份的象徵，反而更像一種束縛。",
