                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The reason is that a uniform does several jobs at once. It makes people instantly recognisable, it signals responsibility, and it gives the public a clearer sense of who is there to help. In many cases, a uniform speaks before a word is said. If you are in pain, in danger, or simply in a hurry, you do not want to play a guessing game about who the right person is. That is why uniforms are especially important in professions where people need to inspire confidence and act quickly under pressure.",
                  "textZh": "原因是，制服其實同時發揮幾種作用。它能讓人一眼認出對方的身份，也能傳達責任感，並讓公眾更清楚知道誰是可以提供幫助的人。很多時候，制服在一個人還沒開口之前，就已經先替他說話了。如果你正處於受傷、危急，或者趕時間的情況下，你不會想玩「猜猜誰才是對的人」這種遊戲。正因如此，在那些需要令人產生信心，並且要在壓力下迅速行動的職業裡，制服就特別重要。",
