                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When a large company does something wrong, the consequences can ripple out far beyond the company itself. It may affect thousands of employees, millions of customers, or even the wider market. On top of that, a small fine that would hit a small business hard may barely make a dent in a giant corporation. If the penalty is too soft, it can become little more than a slap on the wrist, or worse, just another cost of doing business. In my view, punishment should not only be legal; it should also be meaningful.",
                  "textZh": "當一家大型公司做錯事時，後果往往不只停留在公司本身，而是會像漣漪一樣向外擴散。它可能影響成千上萬名員工、數以百萬計的消費者，甚至整個市場。此外，對小公司而言很沉重的罰款，對巨型企業來說可能幾乎不痛不癢。如果處罰太輕，那就可能只是象徵式地打一下手，甚至更糟，只會變成它們做生意的一項成本。在我看來，懲罰不應只是合法，還必須真正有分量。",
