                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "I do not think happiness always arrives with a drumroll. More often, it slips in through the side door in very ordinary moments. When I am with family or close friends, I feel more grounded and more like myself. Good food can also be an instant mood-lifter, especially after a long day, because it brings comfort as well as pleasure. And when life finally goes quiet for a while, it feels as if my mind can breathe again.",
