                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that happiness depends on far more than ability alone. Talent can open doors, win praise, and build confidence, but it can also bring pressure, comparison, and the fear of falling short. In other words, talent may put someone in the spotlight, but it does not guarantee peace of mind. At the end of the day, people are usually happier because of things like love, health, stability, and a sense of purpose, not just because they are gifted.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，快樂取決於的東西，遠遠不只是能力本身。天賦可以替人打開機會之門，帶來讚賞，也能建立自信；但同時，它也可能帶來壓力、比較，以及害怕達不到期望的焦慮。換句話說，天賦也許能把一個人推到聚光燈下，卻不能保證他內心安穩。說到底，人之所以快樂，通常是因為愛、健康、穩定感，以及人生意義這些東西，而不只是因為自己有天分。",
