                  "textEn": "When someone arrives on time, they are really saying, without saying it, that other people’s time matters. In daily life, time is not just money; it is also trust. If a person is always late, even by a little, it can send the message that they are careless, disorganised, or not taking the situation seriously. By contrast, punctuality sets the tone. It makes people seem dependable and helps things run smoothly instead of going off the rails.",
                  "textZh": "當一個人準時到達時，他其實是在用一種不必明說的方式表達：別人的時間是重要的。在日常生活中，時間不只是金錢，它同時也是信任。如果一個人總是遲到，即使只是遲一點點，也可能會讓人覺得他粗心、沒有條理，或者沒有把事情當一回事。相反，守時能替整個情況定下基調。它會讓人顯得可靠，也能令事情進行得更順，而不是慢慢失控。",
