                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Even when advice is well meant, people usually want to feel independent and capable of making their own decisions. So when someone steps in and tells them what they should do, it can land more like criticism than support. In many cases, it is not the advice itself that people reject; it is the feeling of being corrected, judged, or quietly looked down on. Once pride is bruised, even sensible advice can become a hard pill to swallow.",
                  "textZh": "即使建議本身是出於好意，人通常還是希望自己看起來是獨立的，而且有能力作出自己的決定。所以當別人介入並告訴他們應該怎樣做時，那些話聽起來就可能更像批評，而不是支持。在很多情況下，人們拒絕的未必是建議本身，而是那種被糾正、被評價，甚至被人有點看低的感覺。一旦自尊受了碰撞，再合理的建議也可能變得很難吞下去。",
