                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When people are young, they often have to decide what to study, whether to go to university, what kind of work suits them, or even whether to follow a safer path or take a risk on something they truly care about. Those decisions matter because they shape not only future opportunities, but also daily routine, financial independence, and self-confidence. At that age, it can feel a bit like standing at a fork in the road before you have seen the whole map. Of course, no choice is completely set in stone, but some decisions do carry real weight.",
