                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "If parents control everything with too tight a grip, children may become overly dependent, or they may push back simply because they feel unheard. At some point, growing up means learning to think for yourself, make mistakes, and take responsibility for your own choices. Parents should guide the process, not write the entire script of their children’s lives.",
