                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "On the healthy side, a lot of traditional Cantonese-style food is actually quite balanced. There is often an emphasis on steamed dishes, soups, rice, vegetables, and relatively fresh ingredients, so meals do not always have to be heavy or greasy. In that sense, the healthier side of Hong Kong food can feel quite gentle on the body. The problem, though, is that modern city life often pushes people towards quicker, saltier, oilier, and more processed options. So the food culture has one foot in freshness and the other in convenience.",
