                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, if people become too strict or obsessive about food, that can backfire. Healthy eating should be sustainable, not punishing. In real life, balance matters more than perfection. A good diet is not about never touching dessert or cutting out every comfort food under the sun; rather, it is about building sensible habits most of the time. After all, eating well should support life, not take the joy out of it.",
                  "textZh": "老實說，如果一個人對食物變得過分嚴格，甚至近乎執著，那反而可能適得其反。健康飲食應該是可持續的，而不是帶有懲罰意味的。在現實生活中，平衡往往比完美更重要。好的飲食並不是指永遠不能吃甜品，或者把所有令人快樂的食物都一刀切掉；更準確地說，它是指在大多數時候建立合理而穩定的飲食習慣。畢竟，吃得健康應該是為了支持生活，而不是把生活的樂趣都拿走。",
