                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "In recent years, more people have started paying attention to sugar, oil, processed food, and where their food actually comes from. I think that tendency will grow stronger. People may eat less meat, choose more plant-based options, and think more seriously about sustainability, food waste, and long-term health. At the same time, though, it may be a mixed picture. While some people will eat more wisely, others may lean even more heavily on ultra-convenient food. So the future could be healthier in some ways, but not automatically healthier across the board.",
                  "textZh": "近年來，越來越多人開始留意糖分、油分、加工食品，以及食物究竟來自哪裡。我認為這種傾向將來會更明顯。人們可能會少吃肉、多選植物性食物，也會更認真地思考可持續發展、食物浪費，以及長遠健康。不過，同一時間，情況也可能是好壞並存的。一方面，有些人會吃得更有智慧；另一方面，也有些人可能會更加依賴極度方便的即食食品。所以，未來的飲食在某些方面可能會更健康，但未必會全面地自動變得更健康。",
