                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Years ago, education in many places was much more teacher-centred and textbook-driven. Students were often expected to sit still, follow instructions, memorise information, and get the right answers. That approach was not without value, because it built a solid foundation. However, the world has changed, and schools today are under more pressure to prepare students not just to pass tests, but to think critically, solve problems, communicate well, and adapt to change. In other words, the goalposts have moved. It is no longer only about filling students’ heads; it is also about helping them use their minds.",
                  "textZh": "很多年前，不少地方的教育都更以老師為中心，也更依賴課本。學生往往被期望安靜坐好、聽從指示、背誦內容，並且給出正確答案。這種做法並不是毫無價值，因為它的確能打下穩固基礎。不過，世界已經改變，今天的學校面對更大壓力，不只是要讓學生通過考試，還要培養他們的批判思維、解難能力、溝通技巧，以及適應變化的能力。換句話說，教育的目標已經移動了。現在不再只是把知識塞進學生腦袋裡；同時也要幫助他們學會如何運用自己的頭腦。",
