                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "In the past, academic success was often treated as the be-all and end-all, and subjects like maths, science, and language were usually put on a pedestal. Today, while grades still matter, there is generally more awareness that students also need emotional support, creativity, social skills, and even digital literacy. Schools are more likely to talk about mental health, confidence, collaboration, and personal growth. That is probably because modern life is more complex than it used to be. To put it simply, education today is not just about producing good students on paper; it is about preparing young people for a messy, fast-moving, real world.",
                  "textZh": "過去，學業成就往往被視為最重要、幾乎是一切，而數學、科學和語文這些科目通常會被放在特別高的位置。今天，雖然成績仍然重要，但人們普遍更意識到，學生同時也需要情緒支援、創意、社交能力，甚至數碼素養。學校現在更可能談到心理健康、自信心、合作能力，以及個人成長。這大概是因為現代生活比以前複雜得多。簡單來說，今天的教育不只是要在紙面上培養出「好學生」；它更是要為年輕人準備一個混亂、快速變動，而且真實的世界。",
