                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In many schools, students spend a lot of time memorising vocabulary, learning grammar rules, and practising fixed question types. That certainly helps them build a foundation, so I would not say the system is useless. However, language is not a museum piece to be admired behind glass; it is a living thing that people are supposed to use. If teaching focuses too heavily on getting the right answer on paper, students may know the language in theory but still clam up when it is time to speak.",
                  "textZh": "在很多學校裡，學生會花很多時間背生字、學文法規則，以及操練固定題型。這當然有助他們打好基礎，所以我不會說這套制度毫無價值。不過，語言並不是放在玻璃櫃裡供人欣賞的博物館展品；它是一種活生生、要被真正使用的東西。如果教學過分集中於在紙上寫出正確答案，學生就可能在理論上懂得那種語言，真正要開口時卻反而卡住。",
