                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "I believe students learn languages best when they are encouraged to use them in meaningful, low-pressure ways, such as discussions, role-plays, presentations, storytelling, or even casual classroom interaction. After all, people do not learn to swim by reading about water. In the same way, they do not become confident speakers by living inside textbooks alone. If students are given more chances to speak, make mistakes, laugh a little, and try again, the language starts to feel less like a wall and more like a bridge.",
                  "textZh": "我相信，當學生被鼓勵以有意義而且壓力較低的方式去使用語言時，例如討論、角色扮演、簡報、說故事，甚至只是課堂上的自然互動，他們往往學得最好。畢竟，人不可能靠閱讀關於水的知識就學會游泳。同樣地，學生也不可能只活在課本裡，就自然變成有自信的說話者。如果他們有更多機會去開口、犯錯、笑一笑，再重新來過，那種語言就會慢慢不再像一面牆，而更像一座橋。",
