                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Technology moves quickly, and companies are very good at making each new model look irresistible. So people can easily get swept up in the habit of chasing the latest screen, the latest camera, or the latest bells and whistles, even when the difference is fairly minor. In many cases, the purchase is driven less by need than by novelty, convenience, or even status. A phone, for example, can quietly shift from being a tool in your hand to a trophy in your pocket.",
                  "textZh": "科技發展很快，而公司也很擅長把每一代新產品都包裝得令人難以抗拒。所以，人們很容易被捲進一種習慣裡，不斷追逐最新的螢幕、最新的鏡頭，或者最新的功能，即使實際差別其實並沒有那麼大。在很多情況下，購買的動機與其說是需要，不如說是新鮮感、方便，甚至某種身份象徵。以手機為例，它有時會在不知不覺之間，從手中的工具變成口袋裡的獎盃。",
