                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "People now rely on phones, laptops, and tablets for work, study, communication, banking, navigation, and even healthcare. So if someone spends a fair amount on a device that is reliable, long-lasting, and suitable for their needs, that can be money well spent. The real issue is not spending itself, but whether the spending is sensible. In other words, there is a world of difference between investing in a useful device and throwing money at shiny upgrades for the sake of it.",
                  "textZh": "如今，人們依賴手機、手提電腦和平板去工作、學習、溝通、理財、導航，甚至處理醫療相關事情。所以，如果一個人願意花一筆合理的錢去買一部可靠、耐用，而且真正適合自己需要的裝置，那其實可以是花得很值得。真正的問題不在於「花錢」本身，而在於這筆錢花得是否明智。換句話說，為有用的裝置作投資，和單純為了追逐亮眼升級而亂花錢，兩者之間其實有很大的分別。",
                  "pages": [
                    11
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    11,
                    11
                  ]
