                  "labelZh": "總結",
                  "sourceLabel": "Conclusion 2",
                  "textEn": "Overall, I’d say people often do spend too much on electronic devices when they confuse want with need. However, when a device genuinely supports work or daily life, spending money on it is not wasteful at all. The issue in mind is not the technology itself, but the mindset behind the purchase.",
                  "textZh": "總結來說，我會說，當人們把「想要」誤當成「需要」時，他們往往的確會在電子產品上花太多錢。不過，當一部裝置真的能支援工作或日常生活時，花錢在它身上其實一點也不算浪費。總結來說，問題不在科技本身，而在購買背後的心態。",
