                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 6,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "The problem is that convenience can become a crutch. When people rely too heavily on their phones for directions, reminders, communication, shopping, and even entertainment, a dead battery or a bad connection can throw the whole day off balance. There is also the pressure of always being reachable. With messages, emails, and notifications following people everywhere, work can creep into private life and rest can begin to feel like a luxury. In other words, devices do not just sit in our pockets; sometimes they end up running the show.",
                  "textZh": "問題在於，便利有時會慢慢變成拐杖。當人們過度依賴手機去導航、提醒自己、溝通、購物，甚至娛樂時，只要手機沒電，或者網絡不好，整天的節奏都可能被打亂。除此之外，還有一種「隨時都要聯絡得到」的壓力。當訊息、電郵和通知無處不在時，工作就會慢慢滲進私人生活，而休息反而開始像一種奢侈。換句話說，電子設備不只是安靜地放在我們口袋裡；有時它們反而像是在主導整場生活。",
                  "pages": [
                    14
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    14,
                    14
                  ]
