                  "textEn": "From communication and education to banking, transport, and healthcare, computers are a bit like the nervous system of the modern world. Without them, many things that now happen at the touch of a button would become time-consuming and clumsy again. People could still live, of course, but daily life would feel heavier, rougher, and far less streamlined. In some ways, it would be like trying to run today’s world with yesterday’s tools.",
