                  "textEn": "Without computers, people might spend less time staring at screens, scrolling endlessly, or being pulled in ten different directions by notifications. Face-to-face conversation could play a bigger role again, and life might feel a little less rushed and less digitally crowded. In other words, without computers, we might lose a great deal of convenience, but we might also get back a little breathing space.",
