                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "From homework to future jobs, digital tools are everywhere, so it makes sense for schools to help children learn the ropes early. More importantly, school is probably the best place to teach them not just how to use a computer, but how to use it well — for research, communication, problem-solving, and online safety. If children are surrounded by technology outside school but never taught how to handle it properly, they may end up knowing how to tap and scroll without really understanding what they are doing.",
                  "textZh": "從功課到未來工作，數碼工具幾乎無處不在，所以由學校幫助孩子及早熟習這些技能，其實很合理。更重要的是，學校大概是教他們不只是「會用電腦」，而是「好好地用電腦」的最佳地方，包括做資料搜集、溝通、解決問題，以及保護網上安全。如果孩子在校外天天接觸科技，卻從來沒有人正式教他們如何正確使用，那他們最後可能只會點按和滑動，卻未必真正明白自己在做甚麼。",
