                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Traditional performances are not just old-fashioned entertainment. They carry stories, values, language, music, gestures, and ways of seeing the world that have been passed down over generations. In that sense, they are a bit like living archives: they do not simply tell people about the past; they let people feel it. If those performances disappear, a culture can lose not only its memory, but also part of its soul.",
                  "textZh": "傳統表演並不只是老派的娛樂而已。它們承載著故事、價值觀、語言、音樂、動作，以及一代一代流傳下來的世界觀。從這個角度來看，它們有點像活生生的文化檔案：它們不只是告訴人們過去發生過甚麼，而是讓人真正感受到那段過去。如果這些表演消失了，一種文化失去的就不只是記憶，還可能是靈魂的一部分。",
