                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "In today’s world, life can be so fast, fragmented, and screen-driven that people often lose touch with local traditions and with one another. Traditional performances can act as a cultural meeting point. They give communities something to gather around, celebrate, and pass on. To me, that is priceless. A tradition survives not by sitting in a glass case, but by being lived, watched, heard, and felt.",
