                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When you watch a performance live, you are not just seeing it; you are stepping into the atmosphere. You can hear the crowd, feel the tension or excitement in the air, and react in real time along with everyone else. In that sense, a live show has a pulse of its own. By contrast, TV gives you the performance through a screen, so even if the picture is clear, some of the magic can get flattened out. It is a bit like standing in the rain versus watching rain through a window: both are real, but they do not feel the same.",
                  "textZh": "當你現場看表演時，你不只是「看見」它，而是整個人走進了那種氛圍裡。你可以聽到觀眾的反應，感受到空氣中的緊張或興奮，也能和其他人一起即時作出反應。從這個角度來看，現場演出本身就像有自己的脈搏。相比之下，電視是透過螢幕把表演傳遞給你，所以即使畫面很清晰，有些魅力還是會被壓平一點。這有點像你親自站在雨中，和隔著窗看雨的分別：兩者都是真的，但感受並不一樣。",
