                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that water can be polluted in all sorts of ways, from plastic waste and litter to industrial discharge, sewage, and polluted runoff after heavy rain. Sometimes the water may not look terrible at first glance, but that does not mean it is clean. In many cases, the problem is hidden beneath the surface. It can harm marine life, affect water quality, and damage the wider environment bit by bit. So, to me, it is not something we can just brush under the carpet.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，水可以透過很多不同方式受到污染，例如塑膠垃圾、廢棄物、工業排放、污水，以及大雨後被沖入河道或海裡的污染物流。很多時候，水面看起來未必很糟，但那並不代表它真的乾淨。很多問題其實是藏在表面之下的。它會一點一滴地傷害海洋生物、影響水質，並破壞整體環境。所以對我來說，這並不是一個可以輕輕帶過、假裝不存在的問題。",
