                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "A lot of environmental damage comes not from one dramatic act, but from ordinary waste: using too much electricity, throwing away too much plastic, wasting water, or relying too heavily on cars. So if people learn to live a little more lightly, the pressure on the environment can be reduced quite a lot. In that sense, protecting the planet is not always about grand gestures; very often, it begins at home, in the kitchen, at the socket, or on the daily commute.",
                  "textZh": "很多環境破壞其實不是來自某一個特別戲劇性的行為，而是來自日常的浪費，例如用太多電、丟掉太多塑膠、浪費食水，或者過度依賴汽車。所以，如果人們學會讓自己的生活方式「輕一點」，環境所承受的壓力其實就可以減少很多。從這個角度來說，保護地球未必總是甚麼轟轟烈烈的大舉動；很多時候，它其實是從家裡、廚房、插座旁邊，或者每天上班上學的路上開始的。",
