                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that animals are not just there to make the world look nicer. They are part of the balance of nature, and once that balance is broken, the damage can spread further than people expect. In a way, nature is a bit like a woven net: if you keep cutting threads, sooner or later the whole thing starts to give way. So, protecting animals is not only about kindness; it is also about protecting ecosystems that support human life as well.",
