                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, simply pouring money into a problem does not always solve it. What really matters is how the money is used. In my view, it is better to spend it on habitat protection, anti-poaching efforts, rescue centres, and public education rather than on flashy campaigns that look good on paper but do very little in real life. In other words, it is not just about spending more; it is about spending wisely.",
