                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "If schools place too much emphasis on prizes, some children may start to tie their self-worth to results. That is where things can go off the rails. Instead of enjoying learning, they may become anxious, overly competitive, or afraid of failure. Children who do not win may feel left out or begin to think they are simply not good enough, which can be quite damaging at a young age. A prize can be a useful push, but it should not become the whole story.",
