                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The reason is quite simple: when someone has worked really hard and delivered strong results, they usually want to feel that their effort has been seen and valued. A reward is not just a nice gesture; it is a signal. It tells employees, “Your work matters.” In many cases, financial rewards like bonuses are important because, after all, a pat on the back is nice, but it does not pay the bills. At the same time, things like promotion or paid leave can also mean a lot, because they show trust and appreciation in a more lasting way.",
