                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Sometimes the most meaningful reward is not just more money, but a stronger sense that the company believes in you. For some people, being given more responsibility, flexible working arrangements, training opportunities, or the chance to lead a project can mean just as much as cash. A good reward should do two things at once: recognise past effort and open the door to future growth. In that sense, the best companies do not just hand out rewards; they invest in people.",
