                  "textEn": "If people become obsessed with winning at all costs, competition stops being a ladder and starts becoming a trap. Instead of learning and improving, they may compare themselves constantly, feel burnt out, or even cut corners just to stay ahead. In other words, competition is a double-edged sword: it can lift people up, but it can also wear them down if it goes too far.",
