                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "In daily life, people are often so tied up with work and responsibilities that they drift apart without even meaning to. An event like that can act like a bridge: for one evening, people slow down, sit together, talk properly, and pick up old conversations as if no time has passed. I really like that kind of feeling, because it makes life seem a little less rushed and a little more human.",
                  "textZh": "在日常生活中，人們往往都被工作和責任綁得很緊，結果不知不覺就漸漸疏遠了。像這樣的活動其實就像一座橋樑：在那一個晚上，大家都會慢下來，坐在一起，好好聊天，甚至像時間沒有流逝過一樣，把以前的話題重新接上。我很喜歡那種感覺，因為它會令生活看起來沒那麼匆忙，也更有溫度。",
