                  "textEn": "I think many people are drawn to these sports because they are not just chasing a thrill; they are also chasing growth. When someone takes on a real physical or mental challenge, they often discover how much fear they can manage, how calm they can stay under pressure, and how far they can push themselves without falling apart. It becomes a battle not only with the mountain, the wave, or the height, but also with the voice inside their head that says, “You can’t do this.” That is probably why dangerous sports can feel like a rite of passage rather than just a hobby.",
