                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Some activities are risky by nature, such as rock climbing, scuba diving, or skydiving, but people usually choose them knowingly and prepare for them properly. In cases like that, strict rules, proper training, and good safety equipment make more sense than a blanket ban. Otherwise, we would end up wrapping people in cotton wool and taking all adventure out of life. The real issue, in my view, is not danger alone, but uncontrolled danger.",
