                {
                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 2,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that people can easily get stuck in a rut if they only do what feels familiar. New experiences often push people out of their comfort zone, and that is usually where learning begins. Whether it is picking up a new skill, visiting a new place, or speaking to different kinds of people, doing something unfamiliar can shake people awake a little. In that sense, new experiences are like fresh air: they clear the mind and remind people that life can be bigger than their usual routine.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，如果人們永遠只做自己熟悉的事情，就很容易陷入一種一成不變的慣性。新的經歷往往會把人推出舒適圈，而學習通常正是從那裡開始。無論是學一項新技能、去一個新地方，還是和不同類型的人交流，做一些不熟悉的事都能讓人稍微清醒過來。從這個角度來看，新體驗就像新鮮空氣一樣：它能讓頭腦變得更開闊，也提醒人生活其實可以比平日的固定節奏更廣闊。",
                  "pages": [
                    14
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    14,
                    14
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "number": 3,
                  "sourceNumber": 3,
                  "stage": "example",
                  "labelEn": "Example",
                  "labelZh": "例子",
                  "sourceLabel": "Example",
                  "textEn": "For example, someone who decides to learn cooking, join a sports club, or travel somewhere they have never been may discover abilities or interests they did not even know they had. A person who always plays it safe may feel comfortable, but they may also miss out on experiences that could change them for the better.",
                  "textZh": "例如，一個決定去學煮食、加入運動會，或者去自己從未到過的地方旅行的人，可能會發現一些自己原本都不知道存在的能力或興趣。總是凡事求穩的人或許會覺得舒服，但同時也可能錯過一些能讓自己變得更好的經歷。",
                  "pages": [
                    14
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    14,
                    14
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "number": 4,
                  "sourceNumber": 4,
                  "stage": "conclusion",
                  "labelEn": "Conclusion",
                  "labelZh": "總結",
                  "sourceLabel": "Conclusion",
                  "textEn": "So yes, I would say people should try new things, because that is often how they learn more about the world and about themselves.",
                  "textZh": "所以，是的，我會說人們應該嘗試新事物，因為那往往正是他們更了解世界、也更了解自己的方式。",
                  "pages": [
                    14
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    14,
                    14
                  ]
                }
