                  "sourceNumber": 2,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that beginners usually do not know the rules, the rhythm, or what is expected of them yet. When people step into unfamiliar territory, they can feel a bit like a fish out of water. They may worry about making mistakes, looking clumsy, or holding other people back. Once that kind of self-consciousness creeps in, even simple tasks can suddenly feel harder than they really are.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，初學者通常還不知道規則、節奏，或者別人對自己的期望是甚麼。當一個人踏進自己不熟悉的領域時，往往就會有一種格格不入的感覺。他們可能會擔心自己犯錯、動作笨拙，或者拖慢別人。一旦這種不自在和自我意識慢慢冒出來，即使原本很簡單的事情，也會突然顯得比實際上更困難。",
