                  "sourceNumber": 6,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, many new activities come with a learning curve, and that can be frustrating at first. People sometimes imagine they will pick something up straight away, but real progress is usually slower and messier than that. They may get tired more quickly than expected, struggle with coordination, or feel discouraged when they realise they are not good at it yet. In other words, the problem is not always the activity itself; sometimes it is the gap between expectation and reality.",
                  "textZh": "老實說，很多新活動本身都有一段學習曲線，而這在一開始往往會令人感到挫敗。有些人會以為自己很快就能上手，但真正的進步通常比想像中更慢，也更混亂。他們可能會比預期中更快覺得疲累、在協調上出問題，或者當他們發現自己還做不好時，就容易感到氣餒。換句話說，問題未必總是在活動本身；有時候，真正讓人受挫的，是期望與現實之間的落差。",
