                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 6,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "When you do something alone, you have no one to hide behind, so you are forced to rely on your own judgment and adapt as you go. That can be uncomfortable at first, but it can also be incredibly rewarding. In a way, solo experiences strip away the training wheels. They show you what you are capable of when there is no one else to lean on. Sometimes that is exactly what a person needs, not because being alone is always better, but because it teaches a quieter, stronger kind of confidence.",
                  "textZh": "當你一個人去做某件事時，你沒有任何人可以躲在後面，所以你會被迫依靠自己的判斷，並且一路做一路調整。這在一開始可能會讓人不太舒服，但同時也可能非常有收穫。某程度上，獨自進行的經歷就像把輔助輪拿掉一樣。它會讓你看見，在沒有別人可以依靠的情況下，你究竟能做到甚麼。有時候，這正正是一個人需要的，不是因為獨處永遠更好，而是因為它能培養出一種較安靜、卻更扎實的自信。",
