                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "A good party usually lives or dies by the people, the mood, and the sense of connection. If the guests feel relaxed, welcomed, and genuinely happy to be there, even a simple gathering can be a great success. By contrast, a party can be expensive on paper but still fall flat if it feels stiff, showy, or emotionally empty. In other words, money can buy the setting, but it cannot manufacture warmth.",
                  "textZh": "一場好的派對，通常成敗都取決於參與的人、現場的氣氛，以及彼此之間的連結感。如果賓客感到放鬆、受歡迎，而且真的很開心自己來了，那麼即使只是簡單的聚會，也可以非常成功。相比之下，一場派對在表面上也許很昂貴，但如果它讓人感覺拘謹、太過炫耀，或者缺乏感情，那麼它一樣可以很失色。換句話說，金錢可以買到場地和佈置，但買不到真正的溫度。",
