                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that elderly care is too important, too costly, and too demanding to be left entirely to individual families. Love and responsibility matter a great deal, of course, but love alone does not pay for medical treatment, professional care, or long-term support. In many cases, families are already stretched thin with work, childcare, and financial pressure, so asking them to carry the whole burden on their own can be simply too much. In that sense, the government should act as the safety net, because basic dignity in old age should not depend purely on whether someone happens to have a strong family behind them.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，長者照顧這件事太重要、太花錢，也太需要持續投入，所以不能完全交給個別家庭自己承擔。當然，愛和責任感都非常重要，但單靠愛，並不能支付醫療費用、專業照護，或者長期支援的成本。在很多情況下，家庭本身已經被工作、育兒，以及經濟壓力拉得很緊了，如果還要他們獨自扛起全部責任，往往會太沉重。從這個角度來說，政府應該成為那張安全網，因為一個人在老年是否能活得有基本尊嚴，不應該純粹取決於他剛好有沒有一個很強的家庭支撐。",
