                  "textEn": "To be honest, older people do not only need medicine, services, and practical help; they also need warmth, respect, and a sense of belonging. A government can provide structure, but it cannot provide genuine affection in the same way a family can. If elderly people are materially supported but emotionally neglected, something important is still missing. After all, care is not only about keeping someone alive; it is also about making them feel valued.",
