                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In many families, grandparents are a bit like the steady centre of the home. They often help look after children, especially when both parents are working, and they also pass on values, habits, and family stories that might otherwise fade with time. In that sense, they do more than simply “help out”; they help hold the family together. Their presence can be a source of warmth, stability, and quiet wisdom.",
                  "textZh": "在很多家庭裡，祖父母有點像家中的定海神針。他們常常會幫忙照顧小孩，尤其是在父母雙方都要工作的情況下；同時，他們也會把一些價值觀、生活習慣，以及家族故事一代一代傳下去，否則這些東西可能會隨時間慢慢淡去。從這個角度來看，他們不只是「幫幫手」而已；他們其實是在維繫整個家庭。他們的存在，往往能帶來溫暖、穩定，以及一種安靜但有分量的智慧。",
