                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Hong Kong life is fast-paced, and families are not always under one roof anymore, so grandparents may not be involved in exactly the same way as before. Even so, they still tend to be the ones who keep family ties warm. They remember birthdays, hold onto traditions, and remind younger people where they come from. In a world that moves at full speed, grandparents can sometimes be the people who slow things down and bring everyone back to what really matters.",
                  "textZh": "香港生活節奏很快，而且現在很多家庭也不一定再像以前那樣住在同一屋簷下，所以祖父母未必會像從前一樣，以完全相同的方式參與家庭生活。即使如此，他們通常仍然是那群把家人之間的感情維繫得更溫暖的人。他們記得生日、守住傳統，也提醒年輕一代自己是從哪裡來的。在一個節奏飛快的世界裡，祖父母有時正正就是那些能讓一切慢下來、把大家重新帶回真正重要事情上的人。",
