                  "textEn": "To be honest, some jobs may still face pressure from automation, outsourcing, or cost-cutting. If a role is repetitive and easy to train for, wages may remain flat even if the work is tiring. In other words, hard work by itself does not always pay more; what often matters is whether the work is specialised, difficult to replace, or tied to urgent real-world needs. So the future may not lift every boat equally. It may favour the workers whose skills are rare, reliable, and rooted in real demand.",
