                  "textEn": "People often take emotional cues from one another, especially in stressful situations. If a leader, teacher, parent, or even a close friend stays steady, that calm can ripple outward and help other people think more clearly. But if that person panics, loses their temper, or spreads anxiety, the effect can snowball very quickly. That said, I do not think positive energy means acting cheerful all the time. If it feels fake or forced, people can see through it in a heartbeat. What really matters is grounded, genuine energy, not a plastic smile.",
