                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Some children pick up language more quickly, notice patterns more easily, or show unusual memory or creativity from a very young age. So yes, nature does play a part. Still, I would not overstate it. A child may be born with a spark, but it is learning that turns that spark into a flame. Without guidance, challenge, and practice, even natural ability can remain half-asleep.",
                  "textZh": "有些孩子從很小的時候開始，就能更快掌握語言、更容易看出規律，或者展現出不尋常的記憶力或創造力。所以，先天因素的確有它的作用。不過，我也不會把它說得太絕對。孩子也許天生帶著一點火花，但真正把那點火花變成火焰的，仍然是學習本身。沒有引導、挑戰和練習，再好的天賦也可能一直處於半睡半醒的狀態。",
