                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, doing well at school is usually not like flicking a switch. It is more like building something brick by brick. When children listen carefully, ask questions, practise regularly, and keep going even when a subject gets difficult, they gradually become more capable and more confident. In other words, “smart” at school often grows out of consistency rather than magic.",
                  "textZh": "老實說，在學校裡學得好，通常不是像按一下開關那樣立刻發生的事。它更像是一磚一瓦地把東西慢慢建起來。當孩子願意專心聆聽、主動發問、定期練習，而且即使科目變難也不輕易放棄時，他們就會慢慢變得更有能力，也更有自信。換句話說，學校裡的「聰明」，很多時不是靠甚麼神奇天分，而是從持之以恆裡長出來的。",
