                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Some people are naturally curious and like to try a bit of everything, so over time they build up a wider range of skills. Others grow up in environments that encourage them to explore different interests, whether that means sport, music, academics, or social activities. In that sense, becoming well-rounded is often not magic; it is the result of repeated exposure. The more doors a person walks through, the more likely they are to grow in different directions.",
                  "textZh": "有些人天生就比較有好奇心，喜歡甚麼都試一點，所以久而久之便累積出較廣泛的能力。也有些人成長的環境本身就鼓勵他們接觸不同興趣，無論是運動、音樂、學業，還是社交活動都一樣。從這個角度來看，一個人變得全面，往往並不是甚麼神奇的天賦，而是反覆接觸不同事物所形成的結果。人走過的門越多，就越有可能往不同方向成長。",
