                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that family roles used to be much more clearly divided than they are now. Men were often expected to earn the money, make the major decisions, and represent the family in public, so they were the ones who were seen as calling the shots. That idea was tied quite closely to older values about authority, duty, and hierarchy. In other words, the family was often structured more like a ladder than a circle.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，以前家庭角色的分工比現在清楚得多。男性通常被期望負責賺錢、作重大決定，以及在外代表家庭，所以他們往往被視為那個「作主的人」。這種觀念和舊式社會裡對權威、責任，以及長幼有序的價值觀有很密切的關係。換句話說，那時的家庭結構往往比較像一把梯子，而不是一個圓。",
