                  "textEn": "In real life, one partner may know more about finances, while the other may understand the children’s needs more deeply or have better emotional intuition. So it can make sense for husbands and wives to divide decision-making according to who is best placed to judge a situation. That is not inequality; that is practicality. In fact, the strongest families are often the ones where people do not play tug-of-war over control, but bring their strengths to the same table. Two good perspectives are often better than one.",
