                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Traditional festivals are much more than days marked on a calendar. They carry stories, values, customs, and shared memories from one generation to the next. In that sense, they act like a living bridge between the past and the present. Without them, culture can slowly lose its colour and begin to fade at the edges. Festivals remind people where they come from, what their community values, and what should not be lost in the rush of modern life.",
                  "textZh": "傳統節日遠遠不只是日曆上的日子而已。它們承載著故事、價值觀、習俗，以及一代一代流傳下來的共同記憶。從這個角度來看，它們就像一座活生生連接過去與現在的橋樑。如果沒有這些節日，文化可能會慢慢失去色彩，甚至在邊緣一點一點褪去。節日會提醒人們自己從哪裡來、自己的社群重視甚麼，以及在現代生活的急速步伐中，哪些東西不應該被丟掉。",
