                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Modern life can be hectic, fragmented, and a little emotionally thin at times. People are busy with work, study, and endless responsibilities, so festivals create a rare chance to slow down and reconnect. They give families, friends, and communities something to gather around. In many ways, they are a kind of emotional anchor. They remind people that life is not just about deadlines and duties; it is also about belonging, celebration, and shared joy.",
                  "textZh": "現代生活有時節奏很快、很碎片化，而且在情感上也可能顯得有點單薄。人們忙著工作、讀書，以及應付沒完沒了的責任，所以節日正好提供一個難得機會，讓大家慢下來，重新建立連結。它們讓家人、朋友和社區有一樣東西可以一起圍繞。某程度上，它們就像一個情感上的錨點。它們提醒人們，人生不只是截止日期和責任而已，同時也關乎歸屬感、慶祝，以及共同的喜悅。",
