                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Years ago, festivals were often celebrated in a more fixed and local way. Now, people borrow ideas from all over the place, and technology has changed the whole atmosphere. Social media, online messages, video calls, and digital photos all shape how festivals are experienced. A festival today is not just something people celebrate; it is also something they post, share, and curate. That can make it feel brighter and bigger on the surface, but sometimes a little thinner underneath. Still, it would be unfair to say that all change is bad. Modern celebrations can also help people stay connected across distance and make festivals more inclusive than before.",
                  "textZh": "很多年前，節日通常是以一種較固定、也較本地化的方式來慶祝的。現在，人們會從世界各地借用不同元素，而科技更是徹底改變了整個節日氣氛。社交媒體、網上訊息、視像通話，以及數碼照片，都在影響人們如何經歷節日。今天的節日不只是用來慶祝，也同時是人們會發佈、分享，甚至精心呈現的東西。這可能令它在表面上看起來更熱鬧、更盛大，但有時在內裡卻可能薄了一點。不過，若說所有改變都不好，也並不公平。現代的慶祝方式其實也能幫助人們跨越距離保持聯繫，並且令節日比以前更具包容性。",
