                  "labelZh": "總結",
                  "sourceLabel": "Conclusion 2",
                  "textEn": "Overall, I’d say festivals in the past were often simpler, slower, and more tradition-bound, whereas festivals today are usually more convenient, more commercial, and more shaped by technology. However, the core purpose has not disappeared. People still celebrate festivals for the same reason, really: to feel connected, to mark something meaningful, and to bring a little light into ordinary life.",
                  "textZh": "總結來說，我會說，過去的節日通常較簡單、較慢，也更受傳統規範；而今天的節日則往往更方便、更商業化，也更受科技影響。不過，節日最核心的目的並沒有消失。說到底，人們慶祝節日仍然是為了同樣的原因：去感受連結、去標記一些有意義的時刻，以及為平凡生活添一點光。",
