                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, if traditions are presented as a list of rules that must simply be obeyed, many teenagers will switch off straight away. Young people are more likely to engage with tradition when they understand the meaning behind it and are allowed to think critically about it. After all, not every tradition ages well. Some deserve to be preserved, while others may need to be adapted to fit modern life. In other words, tradition should be a living thread, not a chain around people’s ankles.",
                  "textZh": "老實說，如果傳統只是被呈現成一串必須服從的規矩，很多青少年很快就會失去興趣。當年輕人能夠明白傳統背後的意義，並被允許用批判思考去看待它時，他們才更有可能真正投入其中。畢竟，並不是每一種傳統都能原封不動地適應今天的世界。有些值得保留，但有些則可能需要調整，才能配合現代生活。換句話說，傳統應該是一條活生生的線，而不是綁住人腳步的鎖鏈。",
