                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that home is often full of temptations. When people study at home, it is very easy to drift towards the sofa, the bed, the fridge, or their phone. A café, by contrast, creates a kind of middle ground: it is public enough to keep people alert, but still relaxed enough to feel comfortable. In that sense, it gives them a clearer line between “rest mode” and “study mode”. Sometimes a change of scenery is half the battle.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，家裡往往充滿各種令人分心的誘惑。當人在家讀書時，很容易不知不覺就走向梳化、床、雪櫃，或者手機。相比之下，咖啡店提供了一種介乎兩者之間的空間：它夠公開，所以能讓人保持清醒；但同時又夠輕鬆，不會令人太有壓力。從這個角度來看，它能幫助人更清楚地劃分「休息模式」和「讀書模式」。很多時候，換一個環境，本身就已經成功了一半。",
