                  "textEn": "To be honest, friends and family play different roles. Friends are often easier to open up to about things like relationship stress, study pressure, or awkward personal situations, because they are closer to the rhythm of your daily life. Sometimes they speak the same emotional language, so to speak, and that can make you feel instantly understood. A family member may give you depth, but a friend may give you immediacy.",
