                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 2,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that friendship can open a window onto another culture in a way that books or videos often cannot. When you are close to someone from a different background, you begin to understand how they think, what they value, and how daily life looks from their side of the world. That kind of contact can chip away at stereotypes and make people more open-minded. In other words, the world starts to feel a little less foreign and a little more human.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，友情能以一種書本或影片未必做得到的方式，為你打開通往另一種文化的窗。當你和一位來自不同背景的人變得親近時，你會開始明白他們怎樣思考、重視甚麼，以及他們眼中的日常生活是甚麼樣子。這種接觸能慢慢打破刻板印象，令一個人變得更開放。換句話說，這個世界會開始少一點陌生感，多一點人情味。",
