                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In Hong Kong, buying furniture is often tied to a major life change, especially moving house, getting married, or renovating a flat. When people start a new chapter, they usually want furniture that matches their needs, their budget, and the size of the space. In that sense, furniture is not just about tables and chairs; it is part of how a home begins to take shape. A flat may come with four walls, but furniture is often what gives it warmth, function, and a sense of life.",
                  "textZh": "在香港，買家具往往和一些人生大轉變有關，尤其是搬屋、結婚，或者裝修單位的時候。當人們展開新一頁，他們通常都會想買一些符合自己需要、預算，以及空間大小的家具。從這個角度來說，家具不只是桌椅那麼簡單；它其實是家開始成形的一部分。單位也許只是四面牆，但很多時候，真正替它帶來溫度、功能，以及生活感的，就是家具。",
