                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Furniture does not last forever, and people’s needs do not stand still either. A family may need a bigger table when children grow older, a more supportive chair when someone works from home, or extra shelves when the flat starts to feel cluttered. Sometimes people do not buy furniture because they want something fancy; they buy it because daily life has shifted, and the home has to catch up. In other words, furniture often follows life rather than leads it.",
                  "textZh": "家具始終不是永遠都不會老化的，而人們的需要也不會一直停在原地。一個家庭可能會在孩子長大後需要一張更大的飯桌；當有人開始在家工作時，則可能需要一張更有承托力的椅子；又或者當家裡開始變得雜亂時，人們便會想添置更多層架。有時人們買家具，並不是因為想追求甚麼華麗的東西，而是因為日常生活已經變了，而家也需要跟上。換句話說，很多時候是生活在帶着家具走，而不是家具在帶着生活走。",
