                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, patients do not just want to be treated; they want to feel heard. A doctor may be brilliant on paper, but if they are cold, dismissive, or impossible to talk to, patients may leave feeling more anxious than before. A good doctor sees the person behind the symptoms. They explain things clearly, listen properly, and treat people with dignity. Medicine, after all, is not only about curing disease; it is also about easing fear.",
