                  "textEn": "One reason is that modern life is faster, more individualistic, and often more exhausting than before. Many people are constantly rushing, mentally drained, or preoccupied with their own problems, so they tend to keep their heads down. On top of that, people today may be more cautious around strangers because of safety concerns, scams, or simple distrust. So, from the outside, it can look as though people have become colder. However, I do not think the kindness has disappeared; it is just competing with stress, pressure, and caution.",
                  "textZh": "其中一個原因是，現代生活比以前更快、更個人化，而且很多時也更令人疲憊。很多人總是在趕路、精神上被耗空，或者忙於處理自己的問題，所以往往傾向低頭顧好自己。除此之外，現代人面對陌生人時，也可能因為安全顧慮、騙案，或者單純的不信任，而變得更加小心。所以，從表面上看，人們好像真的變冷漠了。不過，我並不認為善意已經消失；它只是正在和壓力、負擔，以及戒心互相拉扯。",
