                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that modern life has made many people more cautious. We live in a world of scams, fake news, online anonymity, and constant warnings about what could go wrong, so it is no surprise that people tend to have their guard up. In the past, life was often more local and more face to face, so trust could grow more naturally through repeated contact. These days, people are surrounded by strangers both offline and online, and that can make trust feel a little harder to give away. In other words, trust has not exactly dried up, but it does not flow quite as freely as it once did.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，現代生活令很多人變得更加謹慎。我們活在一個充滿騙案、假消息、網上匿名，以及各種「小心出事」提醒的世界裡，所以人們會提高警覺，其實並不奇怪。以前的生活通常較本地化，也更常是面對面的互動，所以信任比較容易在反覆接觸之中自然建立。如今，人們在網上網下都被陌生人包圍，這就令信任變得沒那麼容易交出去。換句話說，信任並不是完全消失了，只是沒有以前流動得那麼自然。",
