                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "People may be slower to trust strangers, but they still place a great deal of trust in close friends, family members, colleagues, and communities that feel reliable. In fact, you could argue that trust today has become more conditional than casual. Instead of handing it over at the drop of a hat, people often wait for consistency, proof, or shared experience. That may sound colder on the surface, but it is not necessarily a bad thing. Sometimes trust is stronger when it is built brick by brick rather than given away all in one go.",
                  "textZh": "人們也許不會那麼快去信任陌生人，但他們仍然會對親密朋友、家人、同事，以及那些讓人感到可靠的社群投放很大的信任。其實你甚至可以說，今天的信任已經變得比較有條件，而不是那麼隨手就給出去。人們不再輕易把信任一股腦交出來，而是更常等待一致的表現、證據，或者共同經歷。這樣表面上聽起來也許比較冷，但未必真的是壞事。有時候，信任像一塊一塊磚慢慢砌起來，反而會更穩。",
