                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The most obvious way is academic support. High school can feel a bit like a pressure cooker, with tests, homework, deadlines, and constant expectations all piling up at once. In that kind of environment, students can really help by explaining things to one another, sharing notes, reminding each other about deadlines, or revising together. Sometimes a classmate can explain a difficult point in a simpler, more relatable way than a textbook can, and that can make all the difference.",
                  "textZh": "最明顯的一種方式，就是在學業上互相支持。中學生活有時真的有點像一個壓力鍋，測驗、功課、截止日期，以及各種期望一下子全都壓過來。在這樣的環境裡，學生其實很可以透過互相講解、分享筆記、提醒彼此截止日期，或者一起溫習來幫助對方。有時候，同學能用一種比課本更簡單、更貼地的方式把難點講清楚，而這往往就能帶來很大的分別。",
