                  "sourceNumber": 3,
                  "stage": "example",
                  "labelEn": "Example",
                  "labelZh": "例子",
                  "sourceLabel": "Example",
                  "textEn": "For example, if people want to understand why a country values certain laws, why two groups distrust each other, or why a city looks the way it does, history often provides the missing pieces of the puzzle. Once you know the backstory, the present stops looking random and starts making sense.",
                  "textZh": "例如，如果人們想明白為甚麼一個國家特別重視某些法律、為甚麼兩個群體彼此不信任，或者為甚麼一座城市會呈現今天這個樣子，歷史往往就能補上那些缺失的拼圖。一旦你知道了背後的故事，現在就不再顯得雜亂無章，而會開始變得說得通。",
                  "pages": [
                    22
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    22,
                    22
                  ]
