                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that visual storytelling can bring the past to life in a way that textbooks often cannot. When people see the clothes, the setting, the conflict, and the emotions on screen, history stops feeling like a list of dates and starts feeling like a world that real people actually lived through. In that sense, films and TV programmes can act like a doorway into history: they spark curiosity and make people want to know more.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，影像敘事能以課本往往做不到的方式，把過去活生生地呈現出來。當人們在螢幕上看到服飾、場景、衝突，以及人物情感時，歷史就不再只是年份和事件的清單，而是變成一個真真正正有人活過的世界。從這個角度來看，電影和電視節目就像一扇通往歷史的門：它們能點燃好奇心，令人想進一步了解。",
