                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, filmmakers usually need to tell a strong story, so they may simplify events, combine characters, or exaggerate certain moments to make the plot work. That is understandable, but it also means the version on screen is not always the whole truth. In other words, historical films can show the shape of the mountain, but they may not give you every stone on the path. If people want a fuller understanding, they still need books, documentaries, or reliable sources to fill in the gaps.",
                  "textZh": "老實說，電影創作者通常需要講一個有張力的故事，所以他們可能會簡化事件、把不同人物合併，或者誇大某些情節，好讓劇情更好看。這是可以理解的，但同時也意味著，螢幕上的版本未必就是全部真相。換句話說，歷史電影可以讓你看到整座山的大致輪廓，卻未必能把山路上的每一塊石頭都告訴你。如果人們想有更完整的理解，仍然需要透過書本、紀錄片，或者可靠資料去把空白補回來。",
