                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In the past, learning history often meant reading textbooks and memorising dates, which could feel dry and distant. Now, with documentaries, podcasts, online archives, interactive maps, and even virtual museum tours, history can be brought to life in a much more immediate way. Instead of just seeing the past as a list of facts, people can begin to see it as a story full of people, conflict, change, and consequences. In that sense, technology opens a window into the past and makes it easier for learners to connect the dots.",
                  "textZh": "以前，學習歷史通常意味著讀課本和背日期，這樣很容易讓人覺得枯燥而遙遠。現在，有了紀錄片、播客、網上檔案、互動地圖，甚至虛擬博物館導覽，歷史就能以更直接、更有臨場感的方式呈現出來。人們不再只是把過去看成一堆事實清單，而是開始把它看成一個充滿人物、衝突、變化和後果的故事。從這個角度來說，科技就像替人打開了一扇通往過去的窗，也讓學習者更容易把不同資訊串連起來。",
