                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Everyday life can be demanding, repetitive, and mentally draining. People are often tied up with work, study, family duties, and endless little responsibilities, so after a while life can start to feel like running on a treadmill. A holiday gives them breathing room. It lets them switch off, slow down, and step away from pressure for a while. In that sense, going on holiday is not just about pleasure; it is also about recovery.",
                  "textZh": "日常生活很多時都很有壓力、很重複，而且相當消耗心神。人們常常被工作、學業、家庭責任，以及沒完沒了的瑣事纏住，所以過了一段時間之後，生活很容易開始像在跑步機上不停奔跑一樣。度假能給人一點喘息空間，讓人可以關掉壓力、放慢腳步，暫時離開那些負擔。從這個角度來看，去度假不只是為了享樂，同時也是為了恢復。",
