                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that daily life can easily scatter family members in different directions. Parents are busy with work, children are tied up with school, and everyone ends up living under the same roof but running on different tracks. A holiday can press pause on that routine. It gives people room to talk, laugh, eat together, and actually enjoy one another’s company without always watching the clock. In that sense, a family holiday is not just a trip; it is more like a reset button for relationships.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，日常生活很容易把一家人推向不同方向。父母忙於工作，孩子忙於上學，結果大家雖然住在同一個屋簷下，卻像各自在不同軌道上前進。一次旅行可以暫時按下這種生活節奏的暫停鍵。它讓人有空間聊天、一起笑、一起吃飯，也能在不用時時看時間的情況下，真正享受彼此陪伴。從這個角度來看，家庭旅行不只是一趟外出，更像是替家庭關係按下重整鍵。",
