                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, not every family holiday is picture-perfect. Travel can be expensive, tiring, and sometimes stressful, especially if people argue or have very different expectations. So I would not romanticise it too much. Still, even a short break can do wonders if the atmosphere is right. A weekend trip, a staycation, or even a simple day out can bring people closer, provided that they are genuinely present with one another. In other words, it is not about the postcard view; it is about the human view.",
                  "textZh": "老實說，並不是每一次家庭旅行都像照片裡那麼完美。旅行可能很花錢、很累，有時甚至會有壓力，尤其當大家意見不同，或者對旅程有不同期待時。所以，我也不會把它想得過分浪漫。不過，只要氣氛對了，即使只是短短的休息，也可能很有幫助。一次週末小旅行、一次本地 staycation，甚至只是簡單的一日遊，都可以讓彼此更親近，前提是大家真的把心放在彼此身上。換句話說，重點不在於明信片般的風景，而在於人與人之間的風景。",
