                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 2,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When people travel with others, they often have to compromise on timing, budget, food, activities, and even how long they stay in one place. By contrast, a solo trip means no tug-of-war over plans and no need to keep checking whether everyone is happy. If someone wants to wake up late, wander around for hours, or change course on a whim, they can. In that sense, travelling alone can feel like breathing with your full lungs for once.",
                  "textZh": "當人們和別人一起旅行時，他們往往需要在時間、預算、飲食、活動，甚至逗留多久這些事情上互相遷就。相比之下，獨自旅行就不用在行程上來回拉扯，也不需要不停確認每一個人是否都滿意。如果一個人想晚起、隨意走上幾個小時，或者突然改變路線，他都可以直接這樣做。從這個角度來說，獨自旅行有時就像終於能夠好好呼吸一口完整的氣。",
