                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 6,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Daily life can be noisy, crowded, and emotionally draining, so for some people, being alone on holiday is not lonely at all; it is peaceful. It gives them space to think, reflect, and step outside the usual grind. Sometimes a solo trip is less about sightseeing and more about pressing reset. People may come back feeling calmer, clearer, and a little more grounded. In a way, travelling alone can act like a conversation with yourself, only with better scenery.",
                  "textZh": "日常生活有時很嘈雜、很擁擠，而且相當消耗情緒，所以對某些人來說，假期裡獨處一點都不代表孤單，反而代表平靜。那能給他們空間去思考、反省，並且暫時走出平日的勞碌節奏。有時一趟獨自旅行與其說是為了看風景，不如說更像是在替自己按下重啟鍵。人們回來時，往往會感到更平靜、更清晰，也更踏實一點。某程度上，獨自旅行就像和自己進行一場對話，只不過背景風景更好看。",
