                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In the past, holidays were often simpler and less flexible. People usually had fewer options, less information, and fewer cheap ways to travel. These days, however, people can book flights, hotels, and activities at the touch of a button, so travelling feels far more accessible than it used to. In a way, holidays have gone from being a big occasional event to something people can shape more freely around their time, budget, and interests.",
                  "textZh": "以前的假期通常比較簡單，也沒有那麼靈活。人們往往選擇較少、資訊較少，而且便宜出行的方法也沒有那麼多。不過現在，人們只要按幾下就能預訂機票、酒店和活動，所以旅行比以前容易接觸得多。某程度上，假期已經從一件偶爾才有的大事，變成一件人們可以按自己的時間、預算和興趣更自由安排的事情。",
