                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, not everyone wants a holiday that comes with flights, planning, language barriers, or the risk of things going wrong. Sometimes people are not looking for adventure; they are simply looking for peace. In that case, staying in your own country can make a lot of sense. You do not always need to cross a border to clear your head. A good local holiday can still feel like a breath of fresh air, especially if life has been hectic.",
                  "textZh": "老實說，並不是每個人都想要那種伴隨航班安排、行程規劃、語言障礙，甚至各種變數的假期。有時候，人想要的不是冒險，而只是平靜。在那種情況下，留在自己地方度假其實很合理。要讓自己清空腦袋，並不一定非要跨過國境不可。一個安排得好的本地假期，仍然可以像一口新鮮空氣一樣，特別是當生活一直都很忙亂的時候。",
