                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When people are in a completely unfamiliar environment, even a small problem can snowball very quickly. If they do not speak the local language well, something as simple as reading a train sign, asking for help, or explaining a food allergy can suddenly become stressful. On top of that, if they lose their passport, get overcharged, miss a flight, or fall ill, the holiday can stop feeling like a break and start feeling like a test.",
                  "textZh": "當人處於一個完全陌生的環境時，即使是一個小問題，也可能很快越滾越大。如果他們不太會說當地語言，那麼即使只是看懂火車標誌、向人求助，或者解釋自己對某種食物過敏，這些本來簡單的事情都可能突然變得很有壓力。除此之外，如果他們遺失護照、被人亂收費、錯過航班，或者生病了，假期就可能不再像放鬆，而更像是一場考驗。",
