                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 6,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Every country has its own unwritten rules about behaviour, dress, personal space, tipping, and politeness. What seems harmless to a visitor may come across as rude or insensitive to local people. At the same time, being far from home can make some travellers feel lonely, homesick, or overwhelmed. In other words, the difficulty is not always dramatic; sometimes it is the slow build-up of discomfort that takes the shine off the trip.",
                  "textZh": "每個國家都有自己一些不成文的規矩，涉及行為、穿著、私人空間、小費文化，以及禮貌方式。對旅客來說看似無傷大雅的事情，在當地人眼中卻可能顯得無禮，甚至不夠體貼。與此同時，離家太遠也可能令一些旅客感到孤單、想家，或者吃不消。換句話說，問題不一定總是很戲劇化；有時真正影響旅行體驗的，反而是一點一滴累積起來的不自在。",
