                  "sourceNumber": 7,
                  "stage": "example",
                  "labelEn": "Example",
                  "labelZh": "例子",
                  "sourceLabel": "Example 2",
                  "textEn": "For instance, a traveller may speak too loudly in a quiet temple, dress in a way that is inappropriate for a religious site, or assume that everyone is comfortable speaking English. Even if no one says anything directly, the person may later realise they have made a bad impression. Likewise, on a longer trip, some people start missing familiar food, daily routines, and the people they love, and that homesickness can cast a shadow over the whole experience.",
                  "textZh": "例如，一位旅客可能會在安靜的寺廟裡說話太大聲、穿著不適合宗教場所的衣服，或者以為每個人都很願意用英語溝通。即使當下沒有人直接說出口，那個人之後也可能意識到自己其實留下了不太好的印象。同樣地，在較長的旅程中，有些人也會開始想念熟悉的食物、日常生活節奏，以及自己在乎的人，而這種思鄉情緒也可能令整段旅程蒙上一層陰影。",
