                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In practical terms, everything can suddenly feel unfamiliar. People may not know the transport system, the neighbourhood, the best places to shop, or even where to go for basic services like healthcare or banking. When nothing feels familiar, even small tasks can start to feel bigger than they really are. In that sense, moving to a new place can be a bit like starting a chapter with the map missing.",
                  "textZh": "從實際層面來說，一切都可能突然變得陌生。人們可能不熟悉交通系統、不認識社區環境，也不知道哪裡買東西最方便，甚至連醫療或銀行這類基本服務要去哪裡處理都未必清楚。當周圍一切都不熟悉時，就連小事也可能顯得比原本更麻煩。從這個角度來看，搬到新地方有點像翻開人生新一章，卻發現地圖不見了。",
