                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The problem is that home is not only a place; it is also a feeling of belonging. If people keep moving, they may struggle to form close friendships, settle into a community, or simply feel rooted anywhere. For children especially, constant moving can pull the rug out from under them, because just when they start to feel settled, everything changes again. In that case, life can start to feel a bit like living out of a suitcase.",
