                  "textEn": "I think it depends on a range of factors, such as financial stability, emotional maturity, cultural values, and family circumstances. Some people are ready to move out at eighteen or twenty, whereas others may still be studying, saving money, or helping to care for family members. If people are pushed to leave home too early, they can end up being thrown in at the deep end before they are truly prepared. In that sense, independence is not just about age; it is about readiness.",
