                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "I think that depends a lot on income, timing, and family support. Some couples are able to save for a down payment, especially if both are working steadily, while others may rely on help from their parents to get a foot in the door. There are also couples who prefer subsidised housing routes, because they offer a more stable path than renting forever. So the housing journey can look quite different from one couple to another.",
                  "textZh": "我認為，這很大程度上取決於收入、時機，以及家庭支援。有些夫婦如果雙方工作都較穩定，就可能慢慢存到首期；而另一些人則可能需要父母幫一把，才能真正踏出第一步。也有些夫婦會偏向申請資助房屋，因為那比起一直租屋，感覺上是一條較穩定的路。所以，不同夫婦的住房路線其實可以很不一樣。",
                  "pages": [
                    83
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    83,
                    83
                  ]
