                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that parents are there from the very beginning. They do not just give advice now and then; they shape a child’s world day by day, year by year. Young people often learn behaviour not from what adults preach, but from what they practise. If parents are respectful, responsible, and emotionally steady, those habits tend to sink in quietly and take root. In that sense, parents do not merely guide behaviour; they help build the moral backbone behind it.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，父母從一開始就在孩子身邊。他們不只是偶爾給幾句建議，而是日復一日、年復一年地塑造孩子所處的世界。年輕人很多時候學到的，並不是成年人口頭上教了甚麼，而是他們實際做了甚麼。如果父母待人有禮、做事負責，而且情緒穩定，這些習慣往往就會安靜地滲進孩子心裡，慢慢扎根。從這個角度來看，父母不只是引導行為；他們其實是在替行為背後的品格打地基。",
