                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "However strong online influence becomes, young people are still shaped by the people who know them personally and care about them deeply. A parent, a teacher, or a close friend can sometimes outweigh a hundred online voices, because real relationships carry trust, warmth, and accountability. In other words, the internet may set the mood, but family and community often set the moral compass. So the future influence on young people will probably be a tug-of-war between the digital world and the human one.",
                  "textZh": "無論網上的影響力變得多強，年輕人始終還是會被那些真正認識他們、也真心在乎他們的人所塑造。父母、老師，或者親密朋友，有時候的確能勝過網上上百種聲音，因為真實關係帶着信任、溫度，以及責任感。換句話說，互聯網也許能決定氣氛，但家庭和社區很多時候才是真正定下價值方向的指南針。所以，未來影響年輕人的力量，很可能會是一場數碼世界和人類世界之間的拉扯。",
