                  "sourceNumber": 6,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, as young people grow older, they spend more and more time outside the home, so the people around them start to shape their behaviour in very visible ways. Friends can influence the way they speak, dress, think, and even what they see as acceptable. Teachers, on the other hand, can guide students, correct them, and sometimes become a steady voice of reason. If parents lay the foundations, then teachers and friends often help shape what is built on top of them.",
                  "textZh": "老實說，當年輕人慢慢長大，他們會花越來越多時間在家庭以外的地方，所以身邊的人也會開始以很明顯的方式影響他們的行為。朋友可以影響他們說話的方式、穿著的風格、思考的方法，甚至連他們認為甚麼是可以接受的，也可能受朋友影響。另一方面，老師則能夠引導學生、糾正他們，有時甚至會成為一把穩定而理性的聲音。如果說父母是在打地基，那麼老師和朋友很多時就是在塑造地基之上長成甚麼樣子。",
