                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The gap between wanting something and buying it is already shrinking, and I think it will shrink even more. In the past, people often had to go out, browse slowly, and think things over. In the future, they will be able to see a product online, compare prices, read reviews, and place an order almost on autopilot. In that sense, shopping may become less of a planned activity and more of a seamless reflex. The path from desire to purchase is getting shorter by the year.",
