                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that it gives students fast and wide access to knowledge. Instead of relying only on textbooks or whatever happens to be taught in class, learners can now watch lectures, read articles, join online courses, and look up different explanations of the same topic within minutes. In that sense, the Internet is a bit like a library without walls: it puts an enormous world of information within reach. On top of that, it allows people to learn at their own pace, which can be a game-changer for students who need more time, more practice, or a different style of explanation.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，它讓學生可以快速而廣泛地接觸知識。人們不再只依賴課本，或者只依賴課堂上剛好教到的內容；現在，學習者可以在幾分鐘之內看講座、讀文章、參加網上課程，並查找同一個題目的不同解釋。從這個角度來說，互聯網有點像一座沒有圍牆的圖書館：它把一個龐大的知識世界放到人們伸手可及的地方。除此之外，它也讓人可以按照自己的節奏學習，這對那些需要更多時間、更多練習，或者需要不同解釋方式的學生來說，往往會帶來很大的改變。",
