                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "The problem is that the Internet is a double-edged sword. It offers knowledge, but it also offers distraction, misinformation, and endless noise. If students are not guided properly, they can easily mistake quick answers for real understanding, or spend more time scrolling than studying. A screen can open doors, but it cannot replace discipline, critical thinking, or human guidance. So while the Internet can turbocharge education, it works best when it goes hand in hand with good teaching and good habits.",
                  "textZh": "問題在於，互聯網本身是一把雙刃劍。它能提供知識，但同時也帶來分心、錯誤資訊，以及無窮無盡的雜音。如果學生沒有得到適當引導，他們很容易把「快速找到答案」誤以為是真正理解，或者花在滑動內容上的時間比真正讀書還多。螢幕可以打開很多門，但它無法取代自律、批判思考，以及真人引導。所以，雖然互聯網可以大大提升教育效果，但它通常是在配合良好教學和良好習慣時，才最能發揮作用。",
