                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that the Internet is now woven into so many parts of life, from entertainment and communication to education and daily routines. Children do not see it as some special piece of technology; to them, it is just there, like electricity or television used to be. In that sense, they are born into a wired world. So, instead of stepping into the Internet later in life, they are surrounded by it from the very beginning.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，互聯網現在已經深深融入生活的很多部分，從娛樂、溝通，到教育和日常習慣都離不開它。孩子並不會把它看成甚麼特別高科技的東西；對他們來說，它就只是一直都在，某程度上就像以前的電力或電視一樣自然。從這個角度來說，他們其實是出生在一個高度連線的世界裡。所以，他們並不是長大後才慢慢走進互聯網，而是一開始就已經被它包圍。",
