                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that a lot of work involves routine tasks that do not always need deep human judgment, such as sorting information, answering simple questions, drafting basic content, or spotting patterns in large amounts of data. AI is especially good at that kind of heavy lifting. If machines can handle the mechanical side of work, people may have more time to focus on creativity, decision-making, and human interaction. In that sense, AI could become less like a rival and more like a co-pilot.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，很多工作其實都包含一些例行而重複的部分，未必每一次都需要很深層的人類判斷，例如整理資訊、回答簡單問題、起草基本內容，或者從大量數據中找出模式。人工智能特別擅長處理這類「重活」。如果機器可以負責工作中較機械化的一面，人就可能有更多時間去專注於創意、決策，以及人與人之間的互動。從這個角度來說，人工智能與其說是對手，不如說更像一位副駕駛。",
