                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Some jobs, especially those built around routine and predictable tasks, may shrink or change dramatically. That can leave people feeling uncertain, or even as if the ground is shifting under their feet. On top of that, workers may need to keep learning new tools just to stay relevant. In other words, AI may open new doors, but it may also close a few old ones. So the real issue is not simply whether AI is good or bad; it is whether people and systems can adapt quickly enough.",
