                  "textEn": "The reason is quite simple: technology is not going to disappear, so trying to hold it back is a bit like trying to hold back the tide. The real problem is not the technology itself, but the fact that some people get left behind when change moves too quickly. That is why governments, schools, and employers should offer practical training, digital skills, and career guidance, so workers can move into new roles instead of being pushed out altogether.",
                  "textZh": "原因其實很簡單：科技不會自己消失，所以硬要把它拉住，某程度上就像想擋住潮水一樣不切實際。真正的問題不是科技本身，而是當改變來得太快時，有些人會被拋在後面。所以，政府、學校和僱主都應該提供實用培訓、數碼技能，以及職涯指導，讓勞工能轉到新崗位，而不是被整個系統直接推出去。",
