                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, people can force themselves through a job for money, but only up to a point. If they feel no interest at all in what they do, they may lose motivation, burn out, or start dragging their feet every morning. Interest gives work a spark. It keeps people curious, helps them grow, and makes it easier for them to stay the course when the work gets tough. In other words, salary may get someone through the door, but interest is often what keeps them in the room.",
