                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When grandparents, parents, and children live under one roof, family life can run more like a team than a group of separate individuals. People can help one another with childcare, cooking, housework, and everyday problems. Older family members may pass on experience and tradition, while younger ones bring energy and companionship. In that sense, a multigenerational home can feel less like just a house and more like a built-in support system.",
                  "textZh": "當祖父母、父母和孩子住在同一屋簷下時，整個家庭的運作往往更像一個團隊，而不是一群各自分開生活的人。大家可以互相分擔照顧孩子、煮飯、做家務，以及處理日常問題。年長的家庭成員可以把經驗和傳統傳下去，而年輕一代則能帶來活力和陪伴。從這個角度來看，幾代同堂的家不只是住的地方，更像是一套內建的支持系統。",
