                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Different generations often have different habits, values, and expectations. What feels perfectly normal to one person may rub someone else up the wrong way. Older people may prefer routine and tradition, whereas younger adults may want more freedom and personal space. If people are living on top of one another all the time, even small issues can snowball into bigger arguments.",
                  "textZh": "不同世代的人往往有不同的習慣、價值觀，以及期望。一個人覺得再正常不過的事，對另一個人來說卻可能很刺眼。年長的人也許更重視規律和傳統，而年輕成年人則可能更想要自由和個人空間。如果大家長期都住得很近、幾乎沒有距離，那麼即使只是一些小問題，也可能像雪球一樣越滾越大，最後變成更大的衝突。",
