                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 2,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In a job interview, arriving on time is not just about the clock; it is about what your timing says about your character. If you show up punctually, you seem organised, respectful, and reliable. If you arrive late, even by a short while, you may already be starting off on the wrong foot. Fair or unfair, people are likely to see lateness as a sign that you are careless or not taking the opportunity seriously. In a fast-paced place like Hong Kong, that can really count against you.",
                  "textZh": "在求職面試裡，準時不只是關於時間本身，而是你的時間觀念在替你的性格說話。如果你準時出現，你會顯得有條理、懂得尊重別人，而且可靠。相反，如果你遲到，哪怕只是一小會兒，你也可能已經一開始就失了分。公平也好，不公平也好，很多人都會把遲到看成粗心，或者不夠重視這個機會的表現。在像香港這樣節奏很快的地方，這種印象真的會很影響結果。",
