                  "sourceNumber": 2,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that most people are drawn to things that fit smoothly into real life. If an activity is affordable, convenient, not too difficult, and easy to enjoy even for beginners, it naturally attracts more people. By contrast, if something is expensive, time-consuming, or physically demanding, the crowd tends to thin out quite quickly. In other words, popularity often follows the path of least resistance.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，大多數人都會被那些能自然融入現實生活的事情吸引。如果一項活動價錢合理、方便參與、難度不太高，而且連初學者都能享受其中，它自然就更容易吸引大量人參加。相反，如果某件事很花錢、很花時間，或者對體能要求很高，那麼參與的人往往很快就會少下來。換句話說，受歡迎的東西很多時都會沿著阻力最小的路走。",
                  "pages": [
                    22
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    22,
                    22
                  ]
