                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When my parents were young, leisure was usually more face to face, more outdoors, and in some ways a little simpler. People were more likely to chat with friends in person, play sports nearby, watch television with the family, or spend time on hobbies that did not revolve around a screen. These days, by contrast, a lot of leisure happens online. People stream shows, scroll through social media, play online games, and consume entertainment at the tap of a screen. In other words, the old need to relax is still there, but the wrapping has changed.",
                  "textZh": "當我父母年輕的時候，休閒活動通常更偏向面對面、更偏向戶外，而且某程度上也更簡單。人們較常會和朋友當面聊天、在附近做運動、和家人一起看電視，或者花時間在一些不圍繞螢幕的興趣上。相比之下，今天很多休閒活動都發生在網上。人們會追看串流節目、滑社交媒體、玩線上遊戲，並且只要按一按螢幕就能得到娛樂。換句話說，想放鬆的那種需求其實還在，只是外面的包裝已經變了。",
