                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that films can bring ideas to life in a way that dry facts on a page often cannot. Whether the topic is history, culture, language, or human behaviour, a good film can put flesh and blood on information. People do not just hear about an event or an issue; they see the setting, feel the mood, and understand the human side of it. In that sense, films can turn learning from something flat into something that really lands.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，電影能用一種紙上乾巴巴的事實往往做不到的方式，把觀念活生生地呈現出來。無論主題是歷史、文化、語言，還是人類行為，一套好的電影都能讓資訊變得有血有肉。人們不只是聽到某件事或某個議題，而是能看到場景、感受到氣氛，並理解當中的人性面向。從這個角度來看，電影能把原本平面的學習，變成真正能打動人的東西。",
