                  "textEn": "To be honest, some films simplify events, exaggerate conflict, or bend the truth a little in order to tell a stronger story. That is understandable, but it also means films should not be treated as the last word on a topic. In other words, a film can open the door to learning, but it should not close the book. It works best as a spark, a starting point, or a stepping stone rather than a complete substitute for deeper study.",
                  "textZh": "老實說，有些電影為了把故事講得更有張力，會把事件簡化、把衝突放大，或者稍微扭曲事實。這是可以理解的，但同時也意味著，電影不應被當成某個主題的最終答案。換句話說，電影可以為學習打開一扇門，但不應該因此把書本合上。它最理想的角色，是一點火花、一個起點，或者一塊踏腳石，而不是完全取代更深入的學習。",
