                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 2,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "A documentary is usually grounded in facts, real people, and real events, so it often invites the audience to think more deeply about the world. An entertainment film, by contrast, has far more room to stretch the truth, heighten the drama, or simply take people on an emotional ride. In that sense, documentaries tend to say, “Look at this carefully,” while entertainment films are more likely to say, “Come along and enjoy the journey.”",
                  "textZh": "紀錄片通常是建基於事實、真實人物，以及真實事件之上，所以它很多時會邀請觀眾更深入地思考這個世界。相反，娛樂電影則有更大的空間去誇張情節、加強戲劇效果，或者單純帶領觀眾經歷一場情緒旅程。從這個角度來看，紀錄片比較像是在說：「請你仔細看看這件事」；而娛樂電影則更像是在說：「來吧，好好享受這段旅程。」",
