                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "That usually happens when a film taps into something universal, such as love, friendship, courage, loss, or family bonds. A good film can work on more than one level at once: a child may enjoy the humour and adventure, while an adult notices the deeper message underneath. In other words, the surface may entertain one age group, but the emotional undercurrent can speak to another. That is when a film really earns its stripes.",
