                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "When people are exhausted or under a lot of stress, the mind does not always store information properly. It is a bit like trying to write on water: the moment passes, but nothing really sticks. On top of that, as people get older, memory may naturally become a little less sharp. So sometimes forgetting is not carelessness at all; it is simply the brain asking for rest, space, or support.",
