                  "textEn": "The main reason is that technology is helpful, but it is not foolproof. Phones run out of battery, signals disappear, and devices fail at exactly the wrong moment. When that happens, people cannot afford to realise that they do not even remember a phone number, an address, or a piece of crucial information. In that sense, memory is a bit like an internal backup system: you hope you will not need it, but you are very glad it is there when things go wrong.",
