                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Money can buy comfort, convenience, and opportunity, but it cannot buy every good thing that matters. It cannot guarantee peace of mind, real friendship, or genuine happiness. I think once a person has enough to live with dignity and some freedom, other things begin to matter even more, such as health, relationships, and a sense of purpose. In other words, money is a good servant, but a poor master.",
