                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, money can buy attention, but it cannot always buy respect. A person may be rich and still have very little moral authority, while someone with modest means may carry enormous weight because people trust their judgment. In other words, money can strengthen power, but it does not create genuine influence out of thin air. Sometimes the strongest form of power is not the ability to command people, but the ability to move them.",
