                  "sourceNumber": 6,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "The aim is not to turn them into little accountants or make them think everything in life has a price tag. Rather, it is to help them see money as a tool to be used wisely. If adults focus too much on fear, status, or comparison, children may end up anxious, materialistic, or overly competitive. So the lesson should be about balance, not just about counting coins.",
                  "textZh": "重點不是要把孩子變成小小會計師，也不是要讓他們覺得人生所有東西都可以用價錢去衡量。更準確地說，真正的目標是幫助他們明白：金錢是一種應該被明智運用的工具。如果大人過分強調焦慮、地位，或者和別人比較，孩子最後可能會變得很有壓力、太物質化，或者過度好勝。所以，這個課題真正要教的是平衡，而不只是數硬幣。",
