                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The reason is that letting children make some spending decisions can be a very good way to teach responsibility. When a child saves up for something and then chooses to buy it, the lesson tends to hit home much more strongly. They begin to understand patience, value, and the difference between wanting something for five minutes and really wanting it. In that sense, handling their own money can be a small training ground for adult life.",
                  "textZh": "原因是，讓孩子自己作出一些消費決定，其實是教導責任感的很好方法。當一個孩子辛苦把錢存起來，然後再決定拿來買某樣東西時，那個教訓往往會更真正進到心裡。他們會開始明白耐性、價值，以及「一時想要」和「真正想要」之間的分別。從這個角度來看，管理自己的錢，其實就像是成人生活的一個小型訓練場。",
