                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that the market does not always protect what is culturally valuable. Popular music is often louder, faster, and easier to sell, so traditional music can be pushed quietly to the margins. But traditional music is not just entertainment; it carries language, history, identity, and ways of feeling that modern trends do not always preserve. If a society lets that fade away, it is not just losing old songs; it is losing one of its own voices.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，市場未必總會保護那些真正有文化價值的東西。流行音樂通常更響亮、更快，也更容易被包裝出售，所以傳統音樂很容易在不知不覺間被擠到邊緣。不過，傳統音樂不只是娛樂而已；它承載著語言、歷史、身份認同，以及一些現代潮流未必能保留下來的情感方式。如果一個社會任由這些東西慢慢消失，它失去的就不只是一些舊歌曲，而是自己其中一把聲音。",
