                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, people are much more likely to do the right thing when the legal option is simple, affordable, and easy to use. If official music platforms are reasonably priced and offer a wide selection, then there is far less excuse for piracy. In other words, while piracy is still wrong, the industry also has a role to play in making legal music more accessible. A closed door invites people to climb through the window; an open door makes that much harder to justify.",
