                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Old media usually refers to things like newspapers, television, and radio. Those platforms mainly deliver information from the producer to the audience in a fairly fixed format. New media, by contrast, includes social media, websites, apps, streaming platforms, and online video. It moves at the speed of a thumb swipe. People do not just receive content anymore; they react to it, comment on it, share it, remix it, and sometimes create it themselves. In that sense, old media is more like a stage, while new media is more like a crowded town square.",
                  "textZh": "傳統媒體通常是指報紙、電視和電台這一類平台。這些媒體大多是以一種較固定的形式，把資訊由製作者單向傳給受眾。相比之下，新媒體則包括社交媒體、網站、應用程式、串流平台，以及網上影片。它的速度快得幾乎像手指一滑那樣。現在的人不再只是接收內容而已；他們還會回應、留言、轉發、改編，甚至自己創作。從這個角度來看，傳統媒體比較像一個舞台，而新媒體則更像一個擠滿了人的廣場。",
