                  "textEn": "In old media, content usually goes through editors, producers, or other gatekeepers before it reaches the public. That can make it slower, but it can also make it more structured and, in many cases, more reliable. New media throws the gate wide open. That is one of its greatest strengths, because more voices can be heard. However, it also means rumours, half-truths, and low-quality content can spread like wildfire. In other words, old media may be more controlled, but new media is more democratic — and democracy can be noisy.",
