                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "The problem is that the news cycle can be overwhelming. If people try to consume everything, they may end up drowning in headlines rather than understanding anything properly. So, to me, the real issue is not quantity, but balance. It is better to stay informed in a thoughtful way than to scroll endlessly through a storm of updates. A little clear knowledge is often worth more than a mountain of noise.",
