                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Good discipline is not the same as being soft. In fact, positive discipline can be very firm. It means setting expectations, staying consistent, and responding in a way that protects the child’s dignity while still making the rule clear. It is highly recommended that approaches like calm correction, limit-setting, redirection, and positive reinforcement be adopted rather than hitting or shaming.",
                  "textZh": "好的管教並不等於心軟。事實上，正向管教也可以很有原則。它的意思是，要訂立清楚期望、保持一致性，並用一種既能維護孩子尊嚴、又能把規則說清楚的方式去回應。建議使用冷靜糾正、設限、轉移注意力，以及正向強化這類方法，而不是打罵或羞辱。",
