                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that if children are rewarded with sweets too often, they may start to see sugary food as something special, emotional, or even deserved. That can be a bit of a slippery slope. Instead of learning that sweets are just occasional treats, they may begin to connect them with praise, comfort, or success. In other words, the sweet stops being just food and starts becoming a kind of trophy.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，如果小朋友太常用甜食作為獎勵，他們可能會開始把高糖食物看成某種特別的、帶情緒價值的，甚至是「自己應得」的東西。這其實有點容易一路滑下去。孩子本來應該學會的是：甜食只是偶爾吃的零食；但慢慢地，他們卻可能把它和被稱讚、被安慰，或者成功連在一起。換句話說，那份甜食就不再只是食物，而開始變成一種獎盃。",
