                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "If it is only an occasional reward, and if the child already has a fairly balanced diet, then I do not think it is the end of the world. Childhood should not be so strict that every biscuit feels like a moral crisis. Sometimes a sweet can simply be a cheerful little gesture. The key, though, is that it should stay small and occasional, not become the go-to reward for every achievement, every good mood, and every quiet moment.",
                  "textZh": "如果那只是一種偶爾出現的獎勵，而且孩子本身的飲食已經算相當均衡，那我不覺得這就真的有那麼嚴重。童年也不應該嚴格到連一塊餅乾都像道德危機一樣。有時候，一點甜食真的就只是個讓人開心的小表示。不過，關鍵在於它必須維持在「小」和「偶爾」的範圍內，而不是變成每一次成就、每一次乖巧，甚至每一次安靜下來時的指定獎勵。",
