                  "textEn": "The main reason is that toys are often bought not only out of practicality, but also out of love, guilt, pressure, or the desire to keep children happy. Parents naturally want to give their children the best, but sometimes that can slide into overbuying. A child may be drawn to the newest shiny thing, yet lose interest almost as quickly as they got excited about it. In that sense, some parents are not really buying lasting value; they are buying a burst of excitement that fades very fast.",
