                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "I think that is quite natural, because people tend to throw a party when they want to mark a moment and share the happiness with others. A party is not just about food and music; it is also a way of saying, “This matters, and I want the people around me to be part of it.” In that sense, parties are a bit like emotional bookmarks in life. They help people pause, celebrate, and remember.",
                  "textZh": "我覺得這其實很自然，因為當人們想為某一個時刻留個記號，並且想和身邊的人分享快樂時，就很容易會開派對。派對不只是食物和音樂而已；它同時也是一種在說：「這件事對我很重要，而我也想讓身邊的人一起參與。」從這個角度來看，派對有點像人生裡的情感書籤。它幫助人們停一停、慶祝一下，也把那個時刻記下來。",
