                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The reason is that in Hong Kong, family events are often seen as once-in-a-lifetime moments, so people want to make them look special and memorable. A celebration is not just about food or decoration; it is also about face, family pride, and showing respect to relatives and guests. In that sense, people are not only throwing a party; they are putting on a moment that says, “This matters to us.”",
                  "textZh": "原因在於，在香港，家庭大事很多時都被視為一生一次的重要時刻，所以人們自然想把它辦得特別一點，也值得回憶。這類慶祝不只是關於食物或佈置，很多時也和面子、家庭榮耀，以及對親友賓客的尊重有關。從這個角度來看，人們不只是辦一場派對，而是在呈現一個訊息：「這件事對我們很重要。」",
