                  "stage": "conclusion",
                  "labelEn": "Conclusion",
                  "labelZh": "總結",
                  "sourceLabel": "Conclusion 2",
                  "textEn": "Overall, I’d say spending money on special family events is understandable and can be meaningful, but only up to a point. In the end, what matters most is not how grand the occasion looks, but whether it is filled with love, blessings, and sincerity. If people can celebrate warmly without turning the occasion into a contest, then it is a healthy tradition; if not, it becomes more show than substance.",
                  "textZh": "總結來說，在家庭特別日子上花錢是可以理解的，也可以很有意義，但一切都應該有個限度。說到底，真正重要的不是場面有多大，而是那個場合是否充滿愛、祝福和真心。如果人們能夠溫暖地慶祝，而不是把那個場合變成一場比拼，那它就是一種健康的傳統；否則，它就會變得重形式、多於重實質。",
