                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "From the moment people wake up, they are already making choices. They decide what time to get up, what to wear, what to eat, how to get to work or school, what to prioritise first, and how much money to spend. Most of these decisions may look ordinary, but they are the nuts and bolts of daily life. In a way, an ordinary day is really just a long chain of tiny crossroads.",
                  "textZh": "從人們一醒來開始，其實就已經在作選擇了。他們要決定幾點起床、穿甚麼、吃甚麼、怎樣去上班或上學、先處理甚麼事情，以及要花多少錢。這些決定很多時候看起來很平凡，但它們其實正是日常生活運作的基本零件。某程度上，一個普通日子本身，其實就是一連串細小十字路口組成的。",
                  "pages": [
                    32
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    32,
                    32
                  ]
