                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When you decide on your own, you do not have to explain yourself to five different people, wait for everyone to get on the same page, or sit through a long back-and-forth. You can weigh things up, trust your instinct, and move. That is why solo decisions often feel lighter. A small choice can become surprisingly heavy once too many voices are in the room. In that sense, deciding alone is often the path of least resistance.",
                  "textZh": "當你自己作決定時，你不需要向五個不同的人解釋自己的想法，也不用等大家慢慢達成共識，更不用經歷一大輪你來我往的討論。你可以自己衡量、相信自己的判斷，然後就行動。這也是為甚麼一個人作決定很多時會感覺比較輕鬆。一個本來很小的選擇，一旦房間裡聲音太多，往往就會突然變重。從這個角度來看，自己作決定通常是阻力最小的做法。",
