                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 2,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "At that stage of life, many young people are trying to form their own opinions, make their own choices, and prove that they can stand on their own two feet. So even well-meant advice can hit a nerve. What sounds caring to a parent may sound critical to a teenager. In that sense, the issue is not always the advice itself; it is the feeling of being managed when they are trying to grow into themselves.",
                  "textZh": "在人生那個階段，很多年輕人都在努力建立自己的想法、作出自己的選擇，並證明自己有能力獨立站穩。所以，即使是出於好意的建議，也很容易碰到他們敏感的地方。對父母來說聽起來像關心的話，對青少年來說卻可能像批評。從這個角度來說，問題很多時候未必在建議本身，而在於當他們正努力長成自己時，卻感到自己被人管著。",
