                  "stage": "conclusion",
                  "labelEn": "Conclusion",
                  "labelZh": "總結",
                  "sourceLabel": "Conclusion 2",
                  "textEn": "Overall, I’d say middle-aged people tend to second-guess their decisions because they have more to lose, more to protect, and more life behind them to compare the present with. In other words, they are not simply being indecisive; they are feeling the full cost of choice.",
                  "textZh": "總結來說，我會說，中年人之所以容易反覆懷疑自己的決定，是因為他們有更多東西不能失去、有更多東西需要守住，也有更多已經走過的人生可以拿來和現在比較。換句話說，他們不只是優柔寡斷，而是真正感受到「選擇」這件事背後完整的代價。",
