                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "In real life, problems are often messy and do not arrive with neat textbook answers. That is why teachers, doctors, managers, entrepreneurs, and even engineers often need imagination as well. They may not be painting pictures or writing songs, but they still have to think outside the box, explain things in fresh ways, and come up with solutions when the obvious route leads nowhere. In other words, imagination is not only about art; it is also about seeing possibilities where other people only see walls.",
