                  "textEn": "The main reason is that children usually see the world with fresher eyes. They are less tied down by logic, routine, and the habit of asking whether something is realistic before they let their minds wander. So they can turn an ordinary box into a castle, a stick into a sword, or an empty corner of a room into a whole little universe. In that sense, imagination comes to them almost as naturally as breathing.",
