                  "textEn": "For instance, a child may strongly insist that a rule at school is unfair or that a certain hobby is boring. At first, they may argue just for the sake of it. But after a calm conversation, or after trying it for themselves, they may gradually soften and see things differently.",
                  "textZh": "例如，一個孩子可能會很堅持地覺得學校某條規矩不公平，或者某種興趣活動很無聊。一開始，他可能只是為了爭一口氣而反駁。但在一次平靜的對話之後，或者在自己親身嘗試過之後，他就可能慢慢軟下來，開始從不同角度看事情。",
