                  "textEn": "At first, people often form opinions with limited knowledge. But when they learn more, meet different people, or go through something themselves, the picture becomes less black and white. A view that once seemed rock-solid can soften when reality puts it under a brighter light. In that sense, changing your mind is not always a sign of weakness; sometimes it is simply a sign that your understanding has deepened.",
                  "textZh": "一開始，人很多時都是在知識有限的情況下形成看法。不過，當他們知道得更多、接觸到不同的人，或者親身經歷某些事情之後，整幅圖像就不再那麼非黑即白。原本看起來很堅固的觀點，也可能因為現實被照得更清楚而慢慢鬆動。從這個角度來看，改變想法未必代表軟弱；有時反而只是表示一個人的理解變深了。",
