                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The reason is quite simple: politics is not just something that happens in parliament or on the news. It shapes things like housing, education, healthcare, taxes, and even people’s sense of fairness. So, when an issue hits close to home, people usually feel they have skin in the game. In that sense, giving an opinion is not only about debate; it is also about feeling heard.",
                  "textZh": "原因其實很簡單：政治並不只是發生在議會裡，或者新聞中的事情。它會影響住屋、教育、醫療、稅收，甚至人們對公平的感受。所以，當一個議題和自己的生活息息相關時，人們通常都會覺得自己是局中人。從這個角度來說，發表意見不只是為了辯論，也是在爭取被聽見。",
