                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "These days, people are used to getting things almost instantly. They can order food in minutes, stream a film straight away, send a message in seconds, and search for information at the tap of a screen. When life starts moving at that speed, waiting begins to feel unnatural. In a way, technology has trained people to expect life on fast-forward, so even small delays can feel bigger than they really are.",
                  "textZh": "現在的人已經習慣很多事情幾乎立刻就能得到。他們可以幾分鐘內叫外賣、立刻串流看電影、幾秒鐘內傳訊息，也可以按一下螢幕就找到資訊。當生活長期以這種速度運作時，等待本身就會開始令人覺得不自然。某程度上，科技像是把人訓練成習慣用快轉模式去過生活，所以即使只是一些小小的延遲，也可能讓人覺得被放大了。",
