                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "On the positive side, waiting teaches people patience, self-control, and respect for fairness. In daily life, not everyone can be served first, so a willingness to wait helps society function more smoothly. Whether people are queuing for public transport, medical services, or government procedures, waiting can act like a quiet social rule that stops everything from turning into chaos. In that sense, it is not just delay; it is discipline in disguise.",
                  "textZh": "從正面來看，等待能教人耐性、自制力，以及對公平的尊重。在日常生活中，不可能每個人都排第一，所以願意等待其實能令整個社會運作得更順暢。無論是排隊搭車、看醫生，還是辦理政府手續，等待很多時候都像一條安靜卻重要的社會規則，避免一切亂成一團。從這個角度來看，它不只是延遲，而是一種披著延遲外衣的紀律。",
