                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "If people spend too much time waiting, it can waste energy, damage productivity, and create a great deal of stress. Long queues, delayed services, and endless bureaucracy can feel like sand in the gears of society. Over time, that kind of waiting wears people down. It can make them more impatient, more distrustful, and less satisfied with public life. In other words, a little waiting may build patience, but too much waiting can drain goodwill.",
                  "textZh": "如果人們花太多時間在等待上，它就可能浪費精力、削弱生產力，並帶來大量壓力。漫長的隊伍、延誤的服務，以及沒完沒了的官僚程序，往往就像卡在社會齒輪裡的沙子。久而久之，這種等待會把人磨得很累，令他們變得更不耐煩、更不信任制度，也對公共生活更不滿。換句話說，一點等待也許能培養耐性，但太多等待卻會耗盡人與人之間、以及人與制度之間的善意。",
