                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that patience is not just a personality trait; it is also a habit and a skill. People can learn to pause, manage frustration, and see the bigger picture instead of reacting on impulse. In that sense, patience is a bit like a muscle: the more people practise it, the stronger it becomes. If someone is always taught that everything must happen instantly, they may become short-tempered; but if they learn how to wait, reflect, and stay calm, they are far more likely to grow into a patient person.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，耐性不只是天生性格的一部分，它同時也是一種習慣和能力。人是可以學會先停一停、處理自己的挫折感，以及看到更大的整體，而不是一有情緒就立刻反應。從這個角度來說，耐性有點像肌肉一樣：越鍛鍊，就越強。如果一個人總是被教成凡事都要立刻有結果，他就可能變得很急躁；但如果他學會等待、反思，以及保持冷靜，他就更有可能慢慢成為一個有耐性的人。",
