                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that impatience often comes from frustration with inconvenience, delay, or inefficiency. When people get tired of waiting, repeating the same task, or doing things the hard way, they start looking for faster and smarter solutions. In that sense, impatience can be the spark that lights the fire of innovation. It pushes people to ask, “Why does this still take so long?” and then try to build something better.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，不耐煩很多時候來自對不方便、延誤，或者低效率的不滿。當人們厭倦了等待、厭倦了重複做同一件事，或者厭倦了用很麻煩的方法處理事情，他們就會開始尋找更快、更聰明的解決方法。從這個角度來看，不耐煩可以成為點燃創新的那一點火花。它會推動人們去問：「為甚麼這件事還要花這麼久？」然後開始嘗試造出更好的東西。",
