                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that children are still learning how the world works. They do not yet have the experience, judgment, or self-control that adults usually develop over time. So they may say the wrong thing, trust the wrong person, forget instructions, or act without thinking things through. In that sense, mistakes are almost part and parcel of childhood.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，孩子仍然在學習這個世界是怎樣運作的。他們還沒有成年人通常會慢慢建立起來的經驗、判斷力，以及自制能力。所以，他們可能會說錯話、信錯人、忘記指示，或者在沒有想清楚的情況下就先行動。從這個角度來看，犯錯幾乎本來就是童年的一部分。",
