                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "If children were never allowed to make mistakes, they might become too fearful, too dependent, or too afraid to try new things. A mistake can teach responsibility, caution, and resilience far more effectively than a lecture sometimes can. In other words, children do not just grow by being corrected; they also grow by stumbling, reflecting, and trying again.",
