                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Parents are a child’s first teachers in the deepest sense. At home, children learn how to speak to others, how to handle disappointment, how to show kindness, and how to take responsibility. A lot of that learning is caught rather than taught. Children listen with their ears, but they learn even more with their eyes, because they are constantly watching how adults behave when life is easy and when life gets messy.",
