                  "textEn": "If parents are kind but never firm, the lesson can lose its teeth. Children need to see that actions have consequences, otherwise the message stays soft around the edges and never really lands. The key, I think, is balance: correct the behaviour without crushing the child, and set boundaries without turning the home into a battlefield. Warmth matters, but so does backbone.",
                  "textZh": "如果父母只有溫和，卻從不堅定，那個教訓就可能變得沒有力量。孩子需要明白，行為是有後果的，否則那個訊息就會一直模模糊糊，最後根本進不了心。對我來說，關鍵就在於平衡：要糾正行為，但不要傷害孩子本身；要立下界線，但也不要把家變成戰場。溫度很重要，但原則也同樣重要。",
