                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that without some kind of plan, life can become too reactive. People may drift through the day, lose sight of what matters most, or end up spending all their time putting out fires. Planning does not make life perfect, of course, but it gives people a clearer direction. In that sense, it is a bit like having a map: you may still run into delays or wrong turns, but at least you are not wandering blindly.",
