                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "Some people make plans because they genuinely enjoy structure, while others do it because uncertainty makes them uncomfortable. A plan can calm their nerves and make the future feel less foggy. In other words, planning can be both a tool for success and a form of emotional comfort. That is why careful travellers, worriers, or people who dislike surprises often plan everything down to the last detail.",
                  "textZh": "有些人做計劃，是因為他們真的享受那種有結構的感覺；而另一些人則是因為不確定性會令他們不安。一個計劃可以安撫他們的情緒，也能令未來看起來不那麼模糊。換句話說，計劃既可以是一種通往成功的工具，也可以是一種情緒上的安穩感。正因如此，那些很小心的旅客、容易擔心的人，或者很討厭驚喜的人，很多時都會把事情安排得細緻到幾乎一絲不漏。",
