                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Very often, people start with one idea and then adjust it as they grow older, gain experience, or see new opportunities. A person may discover that what looked right on paper does not feel right in real life. In that sense, planning a future is less like laying down railway tracks and more like steering a boat: you still need a direction, but you also have to respond to the water, the wind, and whatever comes your way.",
