                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Fairly or unfairly, many people associate imported goods with stricter standards, better design, or more reliable performance. When people are spending their hard-earned money, they often want peace of mind as much as the product itself. In that sense, an imported label can feel a bit like a stamp of reassurance. It tells people, “This should be good,” even before they try it.",
                  "textZh": "無論這種看法是否完全公平，很多人都會把進口貨和較嚴格的標準、更好的設計，或者更穩定的表現聯繫在一起。當人們花自己辛苦賺來的錢時，他們很多時候不只是想買到產品本身，也想買到一份安心感。從這個角度來看，進口標籤有時就像一個令人安心的保證印章。它會在你真正使用之前，就先向你傳遞出「這應該不錯」的感覺。",
