                  "sourceNumber": 6,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Sometimes people do not buy imported products only for practical reasons; they also buy them for the feeling attached to them. An imported item can carry a sense of novelty, taste, or even status. It may feel like a small window to another culture, whether that means French perfume, Japanese stationery, Korean cosmetics, or Italian food. In other words, people are sometimes buying not just the object, but the story, image, or lifestyle wrapped around it.",
                  "textZh": "有時候，人們購買進口產品不只是出於實際需要，也是在購買那種附帶的感覺。進口產品可以帶著一種新鮮感、品味感，甚至某種身份象徵。它也可能像一扇通往另一種文化的小窗，不論那代表的是法國香水、日本文具、韓國化妝品，還是意大利食品。換句話說，人們有時買下的不只是那件物品本身，而是包裹在它外面的故事、形象，或者生活方式。",
                  "pages": [
                    6
                  ],
                  "pageRange": [
                    6,
                    6
                  ]
