                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that no country is equally good at producing everything. Some places have more land, some have more energy, some have stronger technology, and some are better at manufacturing certain products. If a country tries to do absolutely everything on its own, it may end up spreading itself too thin and wasting money and resources. In that sense, trade allows countries to play to their strengths instead of forcing themselves to do every job under the sun.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，沒有一個國家會在生產所有東西這方面都一樣擅長。有些地方土地更多，有些地方能源更充足，有些地方科技更強，也有些地方在某些產品的製造上特別有優勢。如果一個國家硬要甚麼都自己做，它最後很可能會把力量分得太散，白白浪費金錢和資源。從這個角度來看，貿易能讓國家發揮自己的長處，而不是逼自己把天下所有工種都一手包辦。",
