                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "If a country puts all its eggs in one basket and depends too much on other places for food, medicine, energy, or other basic supplies, it can become vulnerable when a crisis hits. A war, a pandemic, or even a transport disruption can quickly expose that weakness. So, in my view, the wiser approach is balance: import what makes sense, but still keep enough domestic strength in the areas that really matter.",
