                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that globalisation has brought markets closer together. Improvements in transport, communication, and technology mean that goods, money, and information can move far more quickly than before. As a result, companies are no longer limited to their home market; they can reach customers abroad, source materials from different countries, and build supply chains across borders. In that sense, globalisation has made the world of trade smaller, faster, and more tightly connected.",
