                  "labelZh": "例子",
                  "sourceLabel": "Example",
                  "textEn": "For example, a company might design a product in one country, manufacture its parts in several others, assemble it somewhere else, and then sell it worldwide. That kind of arrangement would be much harder without globalisation. It shows that international trade is no longer just country A selling to country B; it is more like a web, with economies woven together.",
