                  "textEn": "When countries become deeply dependent on one another, a problem in one place can quickly ripple across the system. On top of that, stronger economies and larger companies often benefit more, while smaller firms may struggle to keep up. Globalisation can open doors, but it can also turn trade into a tougher game, especially for businesses that do not have deep pockets. In other words, it creates opportunity, but it also raises the stakes.",
