                  "textEn": "These days, people can get almost anything delivered to their door with just a few taps on their phone. When food arrives quickly, tastes decent, and saves time, cooking can start to feel like the harder option. At the same time, some younger people may not have learnt to cook well in the first place, so they see the kitchen as unfamiliar territory. In other words, convenience has not just opened a door; it has quietly changed the route people take.",
