                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "In a restaurant, food often needs to look appealing, taste bold, and feel worth paying for, so it may be richer, heavier, or more carefully presented. Home-cooked food, by contrast, is often simpler and less showy, but it usually gives people more control over ingredients, flavour, and nutrition. In that sense, restaurant food is a bit like a performance on a stage, while home-cooked food feels more like something built around real life.",
