                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "TV is designed to catch people’s attention quickly. It combines pictures, sound, movement, and sometimes live coverage, so it is very effective for giving people a quick sense of what is happening. Magazines, by contrast, do not need to rush in the same way. They usually have more room for background, analysis, and explanation. In that sense, TV often gives you the headline, while magazines are more likely to give you the fine print.",
                  "textZh": "電視本來就是為了快速吸引觀眾注意而設計的。它把畫面、聲音、動態，甚至現場直播結合起來，所以很擅長讓人迅速知道「發生了甚麼事」。相比之下，雜誌不需要用同樣的方式趕時間。它通常有更多空間去交代背景、分析原因，以及作出解釋。從這個角度來說，電視很多時給你的是「標題」，而雜誌更可能給你的是「細節」。",
