                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "When people watch TV, they usually follow the pace set by the programme, so the information comes and goes quite quickly. With magazines, readers can slow down, reread a sentence, skip ahead, or sit with an idea for longer. That makes the experience more personal and, in some cases, more thoughtful. In other words, TV often washes over you, whereas a magazine invites you to linger.",
