                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that university is very different from school. No one is going to hold your hand every step of the way, so students need to manage their time, keep up with readings, meet deadlines, and stay motivated even when things get tough. In that sense, a good university student is not just a sponge that absorbs information; they are someone who actively engages with it, questions it, and makes something of it.",
