                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The reason is that children learn by trying, choosing, and sometimes getting things wrong. If parents step in at every turn, children may start to doubt their own judgment and rely too heavily on someone else to make decisions for them. In a way, it is like never letting a child ride a bicycle without holding the seat: they may stay upright for a while, but they never really learn to balance on their own.",
                  "textZh": "原因是，孩子很多時都是透過嘗試、選擇，甚至犯錯去學習的。如果父母每一步都插手，孩子就可能開始懷疑自己的判斷，並且過度依賴別人替自己作決定。某程度上，這就像學踩單車時，永遠都有人抓住車尾不放：孩子也許暫時不會跌倒，但他始終學不會真正靠自己保持平衡。",
