                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When children feel watched, corrected, or managed all the time, they may begin to feel suffocated rather than supported. Love is important, of course, but if it becomes too heavy-handed, it can start to feel more like a cage than a shelter. At that point, children may stop opening up, hide things from their parents, or swing the other way and become rebellious just to protect a sense of self.",
