                  "sourceLabel": "Conclusion",
                  "textEn": "Overall, I’d say too much parental interference can hurt both a child’s independence and the trust within the family. Parents should guide, of course, but not run the whole show. Children usually grow best when they feel supported, not suffocated.",
                  "textZh": "總結來說，我會說，父母過度干涉既會傷害孩子的獨立性，也會影響家庭裡的信任。父母當然應該引導孩子，但不應該把整場人生都替他們操控好。孩子通常是在感到被支持，而不是被壓得透不過氣的情況下，成長得最好。",
