                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that advertising shapes attention before it shapes decisions. It puts certain products in front of people again and again, makes brands feel familiar, and often links shopping with emotion, identity, or lifestyle. In that sense, advertising does not always drag people to the shop; more often, it plants a seed in the mind. Later, when people are deciding what to buy, that seed can quietly influence them.",
