                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The reason is quite simple. If people are paying for a service, they usually expect basic respect, efficiency, and a certain standard of treatment. So when the service is rude, careless, or painfully slow, it tends to leave a sour taste in the mouth. Most people do not want to make a scene for no reason, but they also do not want to just grin and bear it if they feel badly treated.",
                  "textZh": "原因其實很簡單。如果人們有付錢購買服務，他們通常都會期望得到最基本的尊重、效率，以及一定水平的對待。所以當服務態度很差、很馬虎，或者慢得令人受不了時，往往就會讓人心裡很不是味兒。大多數人並不是想無端端把場面鬧大，但如果他們覺得自己被怠慢了，也不會願意只是硬吞下去。",
