                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "I think that depends a lot on personality. Some people are very direct and will speak their mind straight away, whereas others would rather keep the peace, leave quietly, and then vote with their feet. These days, another common reaction is to leave a bad review online or tell friends and family about the experience. In other words, even if people say very little in the moment, bad service can still come back to haunt a business later.",
                  "textZh": "我覺得這很大程度上取決於個人性格。有些人很直接，當下就會把自己的不滿說出來；但也有些人寧願維持表面平靜，安靜地離開，然後用行動表態，不再光顧。現在另一種很常見的反應，就是在網上留下負評，或者把那次經歷告訴朋友和家人。換句話說，即使人們當下沒有說太多，差服務之後仍然可能回過頭來影響一家店的名聲。",
