                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is not that older people are less capable; it is usually that they did not grow up with those tools in the same way younger people did. Many young people are used to apps, touchscreens, online payments, and endless updates from a very early age, so using them feels almost second nature. Older people, by contrast, may feel as though the rules keep changing while they are still learning the game. In that sense, the gap often comes from familiarity rather than intelligence.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因並不是長者能力比較低，而是他們並不是像年輕人那樣，在成長過程中一路和這些工具一起長大的。很多年輕人從很小開始就已經習慣使用應用程式、觸控螢幕、電子支付，以及不停更新的系統，所以操作起來幾乎像第二天性一樣。相比之下，長者則可能會覺得，自己還在學習這場遊戲的規則時，規則本身卻已經在變了。從這個角度來說，那道差距很多時候來自熟悉程度，而不是智力本身。",
