                  "sourceNumber": 6,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "If something is designed clearly and people are given enough time to learn it, many older adults can adapt very well. In fact, some of them are far more patient and determined than younger people. The real problem is that many modern systems are built with speed in mind rather than clarity. When buttons are confusing, instructions are tiny, or everything assumes digital confidence, older users are the ones who pay the price first. In other words, sometimes it is not the person that is difficult; it is the design that is unfriendly.",
                  "textZh": "如果某樣東西本身設計得夠清楚，而且人們有足夠時間去學，很多年長人士其實都能適應得很好。事實上，他們當中有些人甚至比年輕人更有耐性，也更肯堅持。真正的問題在於，很多現代系統在設計時重視的是速度，而不是清晰度。當按鈕令人混亂、指示字太小，或者整個系統都假設使用者本身已經很熟悉數碼操作時，最先要付出代價的往往就是長者。換句話說，有時困難的不一定是人，而是那個設計本身不夠友善。",
