                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The Olympics are full of competition, rules, scores, and events that can be exciting if you already enjoy sport. But if you do not care much about athletic performance, it can all feel a bit distant. Some people may not understand the rules of certain events, may not know the athletes, and may not feel emotionally invested in the outcome. In that sense, what looks thrilling to one person can feel like background noise to another. Sport is not everyone’s cup of tea, and the Olympics are sport on a very large scale.",
                  "textZh": "奧運充滿了比賽、規則、分數，以及各種運動項目；如果你本身喜歡運動，當然會覺得很精彩。但如果你對運動表現本來就沒甚麼興趣，那一切就可能顯得有點遙遠。有些人未必看得懂某些項目的規則，也不認識運動員，更不會對結果有甚麼情感投入。從這個角度來說，對一個人而言很刺激的東西，對另一個人卻可能只是背景雜音。運動本來就不是每個人的那杯茶，而奧運更可以說是把運動放大到了很大的規模。",
