                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The Olympics are huge. There are so many sports, so many stories, and so much build-up that some people may feel overwhelmed rather than excited. On top of that, the coverage can sometimes feel repetitive, overly patriotic, or wrapped in too much ceremony. For viewers who prefer something simpler or more direct, the whole event may feel like a circus with too many rings. That does not mean the Olympics are bad; it just means they can be too much for people who like their entertainment in smaller doses.",
                  "textZh": "奧運本身規模非常龐大。項目很多、故事很多、前期鋪陳也很多，所以有些人感受到的不是興奮，反而是疲累和壓迫感。除此之外，相關報道有時也可能令人覺得重複、過分強調民族情緒，或者包裝了太多儀式感。對那些偏好簡單直接娛樂的人來說，整個活動就可能像一場有太多舞台同時在上演的大型馬戲團。這並不代表奧運不好，只是代表對一些喜歡少量、清楚娛樂內容的人來說，它實在有點太多了。",
