                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "These days, many people live busy, fast-paced lives, so they often prefer activities that are flexible, convenient, and easy to fit into a tight schedule. That is why I think sports that do not require a full team, a huge venue, or hours of planning may become even more attractive. In a way, sport is a mirror of life: when life changes direction, sport usually follows.",
                  "textZh": "現在很多人的生活都很忙，節奏也很快，所以他們往往會更偏向那些有彈性、方便，而且容易塞進緊湊時間表裡的活動。正因如此，我覺得那些不需要完整隊伍、不需要很大場地，也不需要花很多時間安排的運動，未來可能會變得更有吸引力。某程度上，運動就像生活的一面鏡子：當生活轉方向時，運動往往也會跟著轉。",
