                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that puzzles develop important thinking skills in a very natural way. They help children concentrate, notice patterns, solve problems, and think step by step. In that sense, a puzzle is almost like a little workout for the brain. Instead of just being entertained passively, children have to look carefully, try different options, and work things out piece by piece.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，拼圖能以一種很自然的方式培養重要的思考能力。它能幫助孩子集中精神、觀察規律、解決問題，並且一步一步地思考。從這個角度來看，拼圖幾乎就像是大腦的一場小小訓練。孩子不是被動地接受娛樂，而是要仔細觀察、嘗試不同可能，然後一塊一塊地把答案拼出來。",
