                  "textEn": "For instance, someone who regularly does crosswords may become quicker with language, whereas a person who practises Rubik’s Cube or other spatial challenges may become better at visualising shapes and movements. If they mix different kinds of puzzles, the training becomes more rounded rather than one-dimensional.",
