                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Talent may open the door, but it does not carry someone all the way through. Sport is full of repetition, pressure, fatigue, setbacks, and moments when progress feels painfully slow. So if an athlete does not have the discipline to train consistently, or the resilience to get back up after a bad performance, their talent can go to waste. In that sense, talent is the spark, but character is the engine.",
                  "textZh": "天分也許能把門打開，但它並不能把一個人一路送到終點。運動本身充滿重複訓練、壓力、疲勞、挫折，以及那些進步慢得令人沮喪的時刻。所以，如果一位運動員沒有穩定訓練的紀律，或者沒有在表現失準之後重新站起來的韌性，那麼天分也可能被白白浪費。從這個角度來說，天分是一道火花，但品格才是真正推動前進的引擎。",
