                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Even in individual sports, athletes usually rely on coaches, trainers, medical staff, and people around them, so they cannot just have a big ego and think they know everything. A strong athlete should be able to take advice, learn from mistakes, and respect both teammates and opponents. To me, the best athletes have fire in the belly, but they also keep their feet on the ground. Winning matters, of course, but so does how a person carries themselves in both victory and defeat.",
