                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that talent may open the door, but it rarely carries someone all the way through it. To reach the top, an athlete usually needs to train again and again, sharpen the basics, and keep going even when progress feels slow. In other words, top athletes are not made in the spotlight; they are made in the quiet hours nobody sees. That kind of discipline builds strength, technique, confidence, and resilience over time.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，天分也許可以幫一個人打開大門，但很少能單靠它把人一路帶到終點。要去到頂尖水平，運動員通常都需要一再訓練、反覆打磨基本功，並且在進步看起來很慢的時候仍然繼續下去。換句話說，頂尖運動員不是在聚光燈下被造就的，而是在那些沒有人看見的安靜時刻裡慢慢練出來的。這種自律會隨時間建立體能、技術、自信，以及韌性。",
