                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "People need to buy food, clothes, services, technology, and all sorts of everyday essentials, and healthy spending helps businesses survive and economies move. The real difference, in my view, is between reasonable consumption and blind consumerism. Buying what improves your life is sensible; buying endlessly just to keep up, fill an emotional gap, or follow the crowd is a different story altogether. So I would not criticise spending in itself. I would criticise excess without reflection.",
