                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that knowledge keeps changing, so memorising facts alone is never enough. Students need to know how to ask good questions, find reliable information, think critically, and solve problems step by step. If they can learn independently, they will not fall apart the moment no one is there to spoon-feed them. In that sense, the real goal of education is not just to fill the mind, but to teach the mind how to move.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，知識一直在變，所以單靠背誦事實永遠都不夠。學生需要懂得如何提出好問題、尋找可靠資訊、進行批判思考，以及一步一步解決問題。如果他們能夠獨立學習，那麼當沒有人再把答案直接送到面前時，他們也不會一下子亂了陣腳。從這個角度來看，教育真正的目標，不只是把東西塞進腦袋裡，而是教會腦袋如何運作。",
