                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that, as people get older, they often become more set in their ways, and learning something unfamiliar can feel less natural than it does when they are young. On top of that, they may be less confident, more afraid of making mistakes, or simply slower at remembering new information. In that sense, learning at an older age can feel a bit like climbing a steeper hill: it may take more effort, but the path is still there.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，隨著年紀增長，人往往會更習慣自己原本的做事方式，所以學習一件陌生的新技能，通常不會像年輕時那樣自然。除此之外，他們也可能較缺乏信心、更怕出錯，或者只是記新資訊的速度慢了一些。從這個角度來說，年紀大了再學東西，有點像是在爬一條更斜的山路：的確要花更多力氣，但路仍然是存在的。",
