                  "number": 2,
                  "sourceNumber": 2,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "A lot of people want quick progress, but skill does not usually work like that. Whether you are learning to draw, play an instrument, cook, or speak a language, you have to keep showing up. One burst of effort may feel impressive in the moment, but it is regular practice that does the heavy lifting. In that sense, improvement is usually less like a sudden leap and more like laying bricks one by one.",
                  "textZh": "很多人都想很快看到進步，但技能的成長通常不是這樣運作的。無論你是在學畫畫、學樂器、學煮飯，還是學一種語言，你都需要不斷出現、不斷練習。一時之間很用力，當下也許感覺很厲害，但真正撐起進步的，往往還是規律而持續的練習。從這個角度來看，進步通常不像突然飛躍，反而更像是一塊磚一塊磚慢慢砌起來。",
