                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, if people outsource every detail to their devices, they may stop exercising their own memory properly. When every number, date, or task is saved somewhere else, the brain can become a little lazy. In other words, technology should support memory, not replace it. Otherwise, people may remember where the information is stored, but not the information itself.",
                  "textZh": "老實說，如果人們把每一個細節都外判給裝置去記，他們本身的記憶能力就可能沒有被好好使用。當每個電話號碼、日期，或者任務都被存到別處時，大腦就可能會變得有點懶。換句話說，科技應該是支援記憶，而不是取代記憶。否則，人們最後記住的可能只是資訊放在哪裡，而不是資訊本身。",
