                  "number": 3,
                  "sourceNumber": 7,
                  "stage": "example",
                  "labelEn": "Example",
                  "labelZh": "例子",
                  "sourceLabel": "Example",
                  "textEn": "For instance, a good doctor does not just know medical facts; they also know how to explain them in a calm and human way. A good manager does not just give orders; they know how to motivate people without talking down to them. That is why communication can quietly make the difference between friction and trust, or between confusion and progress.",
                  "textZh": "例如，一位好醫生不只是知道醫學知識而已；他同時也知道怎樣用平靜而有人味的方式把它講出來。一位好主管也不只是發號施令；他懂得怎樣激勵別人，而不讓人覺得自己被居高臨下地指揮。這也就是為甚麼，溝通很多時候會安靜地決定事情是走向摩擦還是信任，是走向混亂還是進展。",
