                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The reason is that those skills are not learned simply by memorising rules. A person can read about communication or leadership, but that does not mean they can stay calm in conflict, speak with tact, or guide other people well under pressure. In that sense, these skills are difficult because they ask you not only to learn something new, but also to become someone steadier, wiser, and more self-aware. It is one thing to know the theory; it is another thing to keep your head when the heat is on.",
                  "textZh": "原因是，這些技能並不是靠背幾條規則就能學會的。一個人可以讀過很多關於溝通或領導的道理，但那並不代表他在衝突中真的能保持冷靜、說話得體，或者在壓力之下好好帶領別人。從這個角度來說，這些技能之所以難，是因為它們要求你不只是學會一件新東西，而是慢慢變成一個更穩、更有智慧，也更有自覺的人。懂理論是一回事；在壓力來到時仍然能穩住陣腳，則是另一回事。",
