                  "sourceNumber": 2,
                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that science moves faster when minds meet. No single country has all the answers, and many scientific problems are simply too large for one nation to tackle alone. When researchers share data, compare findings, and build on each other’s work, progress can gather real momentum. In that sense, international cooperation does not just add knowledge; it multiplies it.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，當不同的頭腦走在一起時，科學就會走得更快。沒有任何一個國家擁有所有答案，而很多科學問題本身也大到不是單靠一個國家就能解決的。當研究人員共享數據、比較研究結果，並在彼此的工作基礎上繼續推進時，進步就能真正形成動能。從這個角度來說，國際合作不只是增加知識，而是在放大知識的力量。",
