                  "sourceNumber": 3,
                  "stage": "example",
                  "labelEn": "Example",
                  "labelZh": "例子",
                  "sourceLabel": "Example",
                  "textEn": "For example, if someone writes “Fine.” in a message, the reader may start wondering whether that means genuinely fine, slightly annoyed, or quietly upset. In face-to-face conversation, or even on a phone call, that kind of confusion is much less likely.",
                  "textZh": "例如，如果有人在訊息裡只寫一句「Fine.」，讀的人可能就會開始猜，到底那是真的沒事、是有點不高興，還是其實心裡有情緒。在面對面交談，甚至只是講電話時，這種誤會通常都比較不容易出現。",
