                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Not everyone enjoys typing out long thoughts on a small screen. Some people speak much more naturally than they write, and others may not like staring at their phone all day. There is also a generational side to it sometimes. Older people, in particular, may prefer phone calls because they feel quicker, clearer, and more personal. To them, texting can feel like too much tapping for too little warmth.",
