                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "A phone call demands your full attention there and then, whereas a message gives you a bit more breathing room. You can read it when you have a moment, think about your reply, and answer without dropping everything on the spot. In a fast-paced world, that kind of flexibility is gold dust. In a way, a call knocks on the door, but a text slips quietly through the letterbox.",
                  "textZh": "電話通常要求你當下立刻把注意力放上去；但訊息卻會給人多一點喘息空間。你可以在有空的時候才看、先想一想怎樣回覆，然後不需要立刻把手上的事情全都放下。在節奏很快的世界裡，這種彈性其實很珍貴。某程度上，電話像是在敲門，要你馬上應門；但訊息則比較像安靜地從信箱滑進來。",
