                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Some conversations are easier to handle in writing than out loud. If a person feels shy, tired, or unsure what to say, texting gives them time to find the right words. It also avoids that slightly awkward dance of interrupting, talking over each other, or getting stuck in small talk. On top of that, messages leave a trail, so people can check details later instead of relying on memory alone.",
