                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that technology often makes communication faster, but not always deeper. Messages can fly back and forth in seconds, yet tone, facial expression, and real emotional nuance can easily get lost along the way. As a result, people may be more connected on the surface, but less connected underneath. In that sense, modern communication can sometimes become a little thinner: quick to send, easy to miss, and surprisingly easy to misunderstand.",
