                  "textEn": "The reason is quite obvious: those places bring together traffic, machinery, crowds, and constant movement all at once. When all of that piles up, the place can get noisy very quickly. In a big city, the background noise almost never really goes to sleep; it just hums, rattles, and rolls on.",
                  "textZh": "原因其實很明顯：那些地方同時集合了車流、機器、人群，以及不停的流動。一切堆在一起之後，地方很快就會變得很吵。在大城市裡，背景噪音幾乎從來沒有真正睡著；它只是一直低鳴、震動，然後繼續往前滾。",
