                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "Places like schools, restaurants, shopping centres, and even crowded homes can be surprisingly noisy. Sometimes noise follows people indoors rather than stopping at the door. If there are many people in one space, with voices, music, phones, and activity all mixed together, the volume can rise before anyone even notices.",
                  "textZh": "像學校、餐廳、商場，甚至一些住得比較擠迫的家庭，其實都可以非常嘈。有時噪音並不會在門口停下來，反而會一路跟著人走進室內。如果很多人同時在一個空間裡，加上說話聲、音樂聲、手機聲，以及各種活動混在一起，音量往往會在大家還沒察覺之前就已經升上去了。",
