                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When people are running or hiking, they need to stay alert. They may need to hear traffic, bicycle bells, warning shouts, approaching animals, or even the sound of their own footsteps on uneven ground. If the music is too loud, it can wrap them in a kind of sound bubble. In that state, they may miss something important and react too slowly.",
                  "textZh": "當人們在跑步或行山時，他們需要保持警覺。他們可能需要聽到交通聲、自行車鈴聲、別人的警告、接近中的動物，甚至自己踩在不平路面上的腳步聲。如果音樂太大聲，它就會把人包在一個聲音泡泡裡。在那種狀態下，他們可能會錯過重要訊號，反應也會變慢。",
