                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that traffic noise does not come out of thin air; it usually comes from too many vehicles, high speeds, constant honking, and roads that run too close to residential areas. If cities use sound barriers, quieter road surfaces, lower speed limits, and smarter road layouts, they can take the edge off the constant roar. In that sense, traffic noise should not just be accepted as the background music of city life. It can be turned down if the system is designed properly.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，交通噪音並不是無緣無故出現的；它通常來自太多車輛、過高車速、不停按喇叭，以及道路離住宅區太近。如果城市能使用隔音屏障、較安靜的路面物料、較低的車速限制，以及更聰明的道路設計，那麼那種持續不斷的轟鳴聲其實是可以被壓低的。從這個角度來看，交通噪音不應該只是被當成城市生活的背景音樂默默接受；只要制度設計得好，它其實是可以被調低的。",
