                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that an apology is not just a word; it is a sign of self-awareness, humility, and respect for other people’s feelings. If someone never apologises, they can come across as proud, stubborn, or emotionally immature. It may feel as though they would rather dig their heels in than simply admit, “Yes, that was my fault.”",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，道歉不只是一句說話而已；它其實是一種自覺、謙遜，以及尊重別人感受的表現。如果一個人從來不道歉，他往往會給人一種很驕傲、很固執，或者情感上不夠成熟的感覺。那種感覺就像是：他們寧願死撐到底，也不願意簡單地承認一句「是的，這是我的錯」。",
