                  "textEn": "The main reason is that tourists usually do not travel just to see things they could easily find at home. They want something rooted in the place they are visiting — something with local colour, history, and character. Traditional products often carry the fingerprints of a culture, so to speak. They reflect local skills, materials, customs, and ways of life, which makes them feel much more meaningful than ordinary mass-produced goods.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，遊客通常不會只是為了看一些在自己家附近也輕易能找到的東西而旅行。他們想看到的是一些真正扎根於當地的東西——一些帶有地方色彩、歷史和個性的事物。某程度上，傳統產品就像帶著一種文化的指紋。它們反映出當地的手藝、材料、習俗，以及生活方式，所以和一般大量生產的商品相比，往往更有意義。",
