                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that traditional products are not just objects for sale; they often carry local skills, local stories, and local identity. When people buy traditional food, crafts, clothing, or handmade items, they are not only buying a product; they are also supporting local workers and keeping older knowledge alive. In that sense, traditional products are a bit like cultural fingerprints: they remind people where they come from and what makes their community distinctive.",
