                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that people, media, and ideas now move across borders much more easily than they used to. Through travel, migration, films, social media, and international business, traditions no longer stay neatly in one corner of the world. Once people are exposed to another culture often enough, some customs naturally begin to travel, settle in, and take root. In that sense, traditions can spread a bit like seeds in the wind.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，現在人、媒體，以及想法跨越國界的速度和範圍，都比以前大得多。透過旅遊、移民、電影、社交媒體，以及國際商業往來，傳統已經不再安安靜靜地留在世界某一個角落。當人們頻繁接觸另一種文化時，一些習俗就很自然會開始流動、落地，甚至慢慢扎根。從這個角度來看，傳統有點像風中的種子一樣，會飄到別的地方生長。",
