                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "A lot of older products were made more slowly and with more care, so they often feel sturdier and more solid. Whether it is furniture, clothing, or household items, many traditional things were built to last rather than built to sell fast. In that sense, they were not just products; they were almost made with a bit more soul in them. These days, some modern goods can feel a little too disposable, as if they are designed to be replaced before they are truly worn out.",
                  "textZh": "很多舊時代的產品都是慢慢做出來的，也更講究心思，所以它們往往給人一種更結實、更扎實的感覺。無論是家具、衣服，還是家居用品，很多傳統物品本來就是為了耐用而製作的，而不是為了快點賣出去。從這個角度來說，它們不只是商品，幾乎像是被放進了更多心血。相比之下，今天有些現代產品則會讓人覺得有點太「即棄」，好像還沒真正用舊，就已經準備被下一件取代了。",
