                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "To me, traditions are a bit like roots. You may not look at them every day, but they help hold everything in place. Without them, a culture can start to feel thinner, flatter, and more forgetful. Traditions often carry values, stories, and ways of living that have been passed down over generations, so protecting them is not just about preserving old habits; it is also about protecting cultural memory.",
                  "textZh": "對我來說，傳統有點像樹根。你未必每天都會特別注意它們，但它們確實在幫整棵樹站穩。如果沒有傳統，一種文化就可能慢慢變得比較薄、比較淡，也比較容易忘記自己是誰。傳統往往承載著一代一代傳下來的價值觀、故事，以及生活方式，所以保護傳統不只是保存一些舊習慣；它同時也是在保存文化記憶。",
