                  "textEn": "Better technology alone does not solve everything. Transport can become faster on paper but still remain expensive, crowded, or inconvenient in real life. Some places may move ahead quickly, while others are left behind. In other words, progress in transport is not just about speed; it is also about affordability, safety, comfort, and accessibility. If those things are ignored, a shiny new system can still leave people stranded in one way or another.",
