                  "textEn": "When people travel in their own country, however beautiful it may be, the language, food, customs, and surroundings can still feel relatively familiar. By contrast, going abroad can feel like stepping into a different world. People get to hear a different language, see different streets, and experience a different rhythm of life. In that sense, foreign travel often feels less like a short break and more like opening a new chapter for a while.",
