                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that when people are surrounded by different languages, customs, habits, and values, they begin to realise that their own way of doing things is not the only way. That can be very eye-opening. A person who has only ever looked at life through one window suddenly finds themselves standing in a different room altogether. In that sense, travel can make people more open-minded, more curious, and less quick to judge.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，當一個人置身於不同的語言、習俗、生活方式，以及價值觀之中時，他就會開始明白，自己原本那一套做事方式並不是唯一的方式。這種體驗往往非常開眼界。一個原本只透過一扇窗看世界的人，忽然發現自己站進了另一個完全不同的房間。從這個角度來看，旅行能令人變得更開放、更有好奇心，也不會那麼急著去批評別人。",
