                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation 2",
                  "textEn": "To be honest, some people travel but stay inside a kind of comfort bubble the whole time. They only visit tourist spots, eat familiar food, and interact very little with local people. If that happens, the trip may be enjoyable, but it may not really change their thinking very much. In other words, travelling can open the door, but people still have to walk through it.",
