                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When tourists come, they do not just pay for hotels. They also spend money on food, transport, shopping, attractions, and all sorts of small everyday services. That money then flows through the city like blood through the body: it keeps businesses alive, creates opportunities, and helps many people earn a living. So tourism is not only good for big companies; it can also keep small shops, restaurants, and local workers going.",
                  "textZh": "當旅客來到一個地方時，他們付的並不只是酒店費用。他們還會花錢在飲食、交通、購物、景點，以及各種日常服務上。這些錢之後就會像血液流過身體一樣，在整座城市裡流動起來：它讓商業保持活力、創造機會，也幫助很多人維持生計。所以，旅遊業受惠的並不只是大公司；它同時也能讓小店、餐廳，以及本地工作者繼續運作下去。",
