                  "stage": "explanation",
                  "labelEn": "Explanation",
                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "When a city receives visitors from different backgrounds, it becomes a little more outward-looking. Local people may become more open-minded, more aware of different cultures, and more conscious of what makes their own place special. At the same time, tourism can shine a light on local heritage, food, traditions, and landmarks. In that sense, tourism does not only help a city make money; it also helps it tell its story.",
                  "textZh": "當一座城市接待來自不同背景的旅客時，它往往也會變得更向外看。當地人可能會變得更開放、更了解不同文化，也更清楚自己這個地方到底有甚麼獨特之處。與此同時，旅遊業也會把本地的文化遺產、飲食、傳統，以及地標重新照亮。從這個角度來看，旅遊業不只是幫助一座城市賺錢；它也幫助那座城市把自己的故事說出來。",
