                  "labelZh": "解釋",
                  "sourceLabel": "Explanation",
                  "textEn": "The main reason is that ratings make decisions feel less risky. When people are faced with too many options, they naturally look for a shortcut, and ratings often serve that purpose. A high rating can act like a quick signal that says, “This is probably safe, popular, and worth trying.” In that sense, ratings help people cut through the noise instead of feeling lost in a sea of choices.",
                  "textZh": "主要原因是，評分能讓決定看起來沒那麼冒險。當人們面對太多選項時，他們自然會想找一條捷徑，而評分很多時候正正就扮演這個角色。一個高評分就像一個快速訊號，在說：「這大概是安全的、受歡迎的，而且值得一試。」從這個角度來看，評分能幫助人們穿過雜音，而不至於在一大片選擇裡迷失方向。",
